{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3d1201b5-a639-44c0-abb2-e2384a48133d","agentId":"a554eed87317d112b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (FastAPI cuore/). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no commits, minimal grepping. One Edge pass allowed at the end: two 390x844 screenshots (iPhone size) via the CDP pattern in cuore/tests/check_bench.py against your own temp-state server, cleanup via cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py. Report under 120 words. Another agent is building cuore/services/vision_bridge.py, cuore/api/vision.py and cuore/tests/check_vision.py: do not create those; you consume a contract described below. You own cuore/web/owner_routes.py, templates/m_*.html, static/m.css, static/m.js (new), cuore/tests/check_owner_page.py, cuore/web/i18n.py (additive).\n\nThe owner rejected the current Mobile surface (/m/{vin}): \"not up to the graphical and prestige standards of the passion CUORE was built upon; easier, more graphical, fewer clicks, dark theme, take a picture of the odometer / oil bottle / gas pump and fill in the questions automatically; open with the slow CUORE introduction the main app uses.\" Rebuild it to the Ferrari-page benchmark the main app follows (see cuore/web/static/cuore.css \"Emphasis pass\" comment and the marque theme: true black, one statement per screen, big figures, red reserved for the one primary action, 16-17px body, 48px targets, pictograms from static/icons.svg):\n1. Opening reveal: reuse cuore/web/templates/_intro.html and its .intro-overlay CSS (include it in m_base.html; same timing, dismiss on tap, play on every open of /m/{vin} as the owner asked, not once per session).\n2. Home (/m/{vin}): hero with vehicle display name (same resolver the other routes use: shop_bridge.resolve_vehicle_name), odometer last known, and the car's verdict in one line; then 4 big quick actions, one tap to a form: Fill-up, Oil & fluids, Battery & electrical, Snap & fill (camera); then unread Messages count badge; then \"Everything else\" tiles for the remaining categories. Bottom nav stays (Add · Messages · History) but 56px, pictograms + labels.\n3. Fewer taps on the fill-up form (/m/{vin}/add/fuel/fill_up): station chip row preselects the last used (remembered values already exist via recents), octane as 48px chips with the last used preselected, litres and price big numeric inputs with inputmode=decimal, \"cap clicked\" default yes as a large toggle, odometer optional; Save is the only red button; after save a full-screen confirmation with the recorded card and \"Add another\" / \"Done\". A whole fill-up must be possible in 3 taps when nothing changed from last time.\n4. Camera everywhere: every form gets a \"Take a photo\" tile at the top (`<input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\" capture=\"environment\">`, works in iOS Safari), preview inline, uploaded through the existing media API (grep -l \"def upload\\|@router.post\" cuore/api/media.py once; link the media id into the event's media_ids). Snap & fill: a dedicated screen /m/{vin}/snap: take the photo, POST it to the vision contract `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read` as multipart form field \"file\" plus \"hint\" (one of odometer|fuel_pump|oil_bottle|part_label|receipt|other); response JSON {provider, available: bool, fields: {name: {value, confidence, unit}}, suggested_kind: \"category/kind\"|null, note}. If available is false, show \"Automatic reading is not set up on this CUORE; fill in by hand\" and continue to the kind picker with the photo attached. If fields come back, open that kind's form prefilled with the values marked \"read from photo — check before saving\" (amber chip on each prefilled field; the save stores them as attested, with fields_source: \"photo\" for those keys — pass a hidden input `source_<key>=photo` the route records into the event's fields_meta). Never save without the human tapping Save.\n5. m.js (small, no framework): intro dismiss, chip → input fill, photo preview, snap flow, toast. Everything must still work without JS except the snap auto-fill.\n6. Dark only on mobile (color-scheme dark), marque accent from data-marque, no font under 12px, nothing clipped at 390px, no horizontal scroll.\n7. Tests (extend check_owner_page.py, TestClient): home shows the 4 quick actions and the intro overlay markup; fill-up form shows octane chips with the last used preselected after one prior fill-up; snap page renders with the file input and capture attribute; a POST with source_octane=photo stores fields_meta.octane == \"photo\"; the vision endpoint being absent (404) is handled by the page (test the route guards). Run it plus check_screens.py."},"uuid":"33ac99b8-6a84-4c51-88a8-239eddf22f1d","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:54:08.559Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
