{"parentUuid":"9f035292-d967-4663-af4a-4b739f419020","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a554eed87317d112b","attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"Owner's note just now: \"design and finish is important.\" Raise the bar on the Mobile rebuild accordingly: this is the one surface the owner holds in their hand at a pump, so it must read as CUORE, not a web form. Concretely: true black, generous whitespace, one statement per screen; the hero's vehicle name in the marque display weight (300) at 32-40px with the odometer as a big tabular figure and a small-caps label; quick-action tiles as full-bleed cards with the pictogram at 40px, a single red card for the primary action only; chips with 12px letter-spaced small-caps labels and selected state in the marque accent; inputs as large underlined fields (no boxes), units set small after the figure; the confirmation screen as a \"record card\" with a thin rule, the date, and the attested footer line; transitions: 200ms ease on the chips and a fade on the confirmation; the intro reveal timing identical to the main app. No default browser buttons, no blue links, no generic grey. Take the two 390x844 screenshots at the end and judge them against the Ferrari benchmark before reporting; if they look like a form, iterate once more.","source_uuid":"1233b052-dbd5-4ade-a888-1fa6a2ff1386","origin":{"kind":"coordinator"},"isMeta":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"01b31ce8-9b00-4065-a9b3-3f67324d9c6f","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:56:05.817Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe coordinator sent a message while you were working:\nOwner's note just now: \"design and finish is important.\" Raise the bar on the Mobile rebuild accordingly: this is the one surface the owner holds in their hand at a pump, so it must read as CUORE, not a web form. Concretely: true black, generous whitespace, one statement per screen; the hero's vehicle name in the marque display weight (300) at 32-40px with the odometer as a big tabular figure and a small-caps label; quick-action tiles as full-bleed cards with the pictogram at 40px, a single red card for the primary action only; chips with 12px letter-spaced small-caps labels and selected state in the marque accent; inputs as large underlined fields (no boxes), units set small after the figure; the confirmation screen as a \"record card\" with a thin rule, the date, and the attested footer line; transitions: 200ms ease on the chips and a fade on the confirmation; the intro reveal timing identical to the main app. No default browser buttons, no blue links, no generic grey. Take the two 390x844 screenshots at the end and judge them against the Ferrari benchmark before reporting; if they look like a form, iterate once more.\n\nAddress this before completing your current task.\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
