{"parentUuid":"586a6251-e302-463d-a16b-35499bc2d235","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a554eed87317d112b","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfzv9cf6e3Yyga8QpmpCK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TKMx7wgP3Yu7geX5vxzCyY","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\live\\owner_events.py","old_string":"``fields_meta`` (added 2026-10-13, additive -- older rows simply have none)\nis ``{field_key: \"photo\"}`` for any field whose value was read off a photo\nby the Mobile \"Snap & fill\" screen (``cuore.web.owner_routes``) rather than\ntyped by the person -- see that module's own docstring for the contract\nwith ``cuore.services.vision_bridge``. It is informational only: a\nphoto-read field is stored at the same ``confidence: \"reported\"`` as every\nother owner-typed value (a human still tapped Save), this just remembers\n*how* the value got into the box, for the \"check before saving\" amber chip\nand for anyone auditing the report later.","new_string":"``fields_meta`` (added 2026-10-13, additive -- older rows simply have none)\nis ``{field_key: \"photo\"|\"typed\"}``, one entry per field whose provenance\nis worth remembering -- \"photo\" for a value read off a picture by the\nMobile \"Snap & fill\" screen (``cuore.web.owner_routes``) rather than typed\nby the person, \"typed\" for an explicit hand-entry note; see that module's\nown docstring, and ``cuore.api.owner_events``, for the two callers (the\nHTML form's ``source_<key>=photo`` hidden inputs, and the JSON API's own\n``fields_meta`` body key) that both feed this same parameter. Only a key\nthat is (a) one of this kind's real taxonomy fields and (b) one of these\ntwo words survives into the stored row -- anything else is dropped\nsilently, same posture as an unknown field key ever since this store\nexisted. It is informational only: a photo-read field is stored at the\nsame ``confidence: \"reported\"`` as every other owner-typed value (a human\nstill tapped Save) -- this just remembers *how* the value got into the\nbox, for the \"check before saving\" amber chip and for anyone auditing the\nreport later."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":688,"cache_read_input_tokens":199853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":688,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TKMx7wgP3Yu7geX5vxzCyY":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\live\\owner_events.py","old_string":"``fields_meta`` (added 2026-10-13, additive -- older rows simply have none)\nis ``{field_key: \"photo\"}`` for any field whose value was read off a photo\nby the Mobile \"Snap & fill\" screen (``cuore.web.owner_routes``) rather than\ntyped by the person -- see that module's own docstring for the contract\nwith ``cuore.services.vision_bridge``. It is informational only: a\nphoto-read field is stored at the same ``confidence: \"reported\"`` as every\nother owner-typed value (a human still tapped Save), this just remembers\n*how* the value got into the box, for the \"check before saving\" amber chip\nand for anyone auditing the report later.","new_string":"``fields_meta`` (added 2026-10-13, additive -- older rows simply have none)\nis ``{field_key: \"photo\"|\"typed\"}``, one entry per field whose provenance\nis worth remembering -- \"photo\" for a value read off a picture by the\nMobile \"Snap & fill\" screen (``cuore.web.owner_routes``) rather than typed\nby the person, \"typed\" for an explicit hand-entry note; see that module's\nown docstring, and ``cuore.api.owner_events``, for the two callers (the\nHTML form's ``source_<key>=photo`` hidden inputs, and the JSON API's own\n``fields_meta`` body key) that both feed th