{"parentUuid":"2ffd3cfa-f0e4-4df4-9f28-d6248c042fab","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a554eed87317d112b","attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_013DdMotD16JKgfB3nZMCPLK","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c0227edc-21f4-4630-b936-7bff69c59cf7","timestamp":"2026-10-13T22:54:50.274Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"c0227edc-21f4-4630-b936-7bff69c59cf7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a554eed87317d112b","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg14MXfV5FNmcfFDTPoCy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1552,"cache_read_input_tokens":215780,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1552,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7e8d9abe-161f-4bde-bda4-77c024180239","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cg14MXPcDe7hPbNRh9ZtY","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"91138f77-4ebc-4233-a42d-34fbd741c94f","timestamp":"2026-10-13T22:54:50.273Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"91138f77-4ebc-4233-a42d-34fbd741c94f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a554eed87317d112b","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg14MXfV5FNmcfFDTPoCy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TE9xGgCwUJduRHpgzYqVXf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\owner_routes.py","content":"\"\"\"``/m/{vin}`` -- \"Tell CUORE\": the phone-first page where an owner, driver\nor mechanic records what the car cannot discover on its own, and reads\nmessages/questions from CUORE and the mechanic.\n\nRebuilt 2026-10-13 to the Ferrari-page benchmark the main app follows (see\n``cuore/web/static/cuore.css``'s \"Emphasis pass\" section) after the owner\nrejected the first pass as \"not up to the graphical and prestige standards\n... CUORE was built upon\". Still its own minimal layout (``templates/\nm_*.html``, own ``Jinja2Templates`` instance, no desktop tabs/hero, no\ndependency on ``cuore.web.routes``'s shared chrome) -- just a phone-width\npage with a bottom nav (Add / Messages / History), now hero-first with four\none-tap quick actions and a camera on every form.\n\n**Every record this page writes is ATTESTED, never a car measurement** --\nsee ``cuore/live/owner_events.py``'s docstring. The one-line footer on every\npage here says the same thing; do not remove it if these templates are\nedited later.\n\nWorks without JavaScript for everything except the \"Snap & fill\" photo\nauto-read: every form is a plain ``<form method=\"post\">`` (``enctype=\n\"multipart/form-data\"`` wherever a photo tile is present) that redirects on\nsuccess -- the camera tile, the fill-up flow and the Snap screen's own\n``Continue`` button all submit fine with scripting off; ``m.js`` only adds\nthe inline photo preview and the client-side call to\n``POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`` that can skip straight to a prefilled form.\nSame no-JS convention ``cuore.web.media_routes.media_upload`` and\n``inbox_routes`` use.\n\nPhoto contract with ``cuore.services.vision_bridge`` (built by another\nagent, now live as ``cuore.api.vision``): this module never calls it from\nPython -- only ``m.js`` does, client-side, against\n``POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`` (multipart ``file`` + ``hint``, one of\n:data:`SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET`'s keys). The response is\n``{provider, available, fields: {key: {value, confidence, unit}},\nsuggested_kind: \"category/kind\"|None, note}``. When it comes back usable,\n``m.js`` navigates straight to that kind's ``GET`` form with the read\nvalues and ``source_<key>=photo`` on the query string; :func:`add_form`\nturns those into the amber \"read from photo\" prefill, and\n:func:`add_submit` turns a submitted ``source_<key>=photo`` into\n``fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"`` on the stored event (the same provenance tag\nthe JSON API's ``POST /owner/{vin}/events`` body now also accepts, so a\nnative app can mark the same thing). When the endpoint is 404 (not wired\nup yet), unreachable, or answers ``available: false``, the **same** POST\n``/m/{vin}/snap`` this page already posts to without any JS at all is what\nthe person lands on -- there is no server-side dependency on vision ever\nsucceeding.\n\nRegistration note: ``cuore/app.py`` is owned by another agent. The one line\nneeded there, beside the other ``web`` routers::\n\n    app.include_router(owner_routes.router)\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport socket\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, RedirectResponse\nfrom fastapi.templating import Jinja2Templates\n\nfrom ..api.deps import require_token, settings_of\nfrom ..live import media as media_store\nfrom ..live import owner_events as store\nfrom ..services import dossier_bridge, mes_bridge, owner_events_bridge as bridge, shop_bridge\nfrom ..services.errors import BridgeError\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nTEMPLATE_DIR = HERE / \"templates\"\n\ntemplates = Jinja2Templates(directory=str(TEMPLATE_DIR))\n\nrouter = APIRouter(include_in_schema=False, dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n\n#: One pictogram-free label per category -- ``static/icons.svg`` has no\n#: symbol for any of these nine categories (its ``i-sys_*``/``i-symptom_*``\n#: set covers the systems graph and the driver symptom vocabulary, not\n#: owner-reported maintenance categories), so tiles render as plain labelled\n#: rows rather than inventing icons that would not match that file's house\n#: style. Flagged here rather than silently -- see the task note this\n#: satisfies.\nCATEGORY_ORDER = (\"fluids\", \"fuel\", \"battery_electrical\", \"tyres_wheels_brakes\",\n                  \"parts_repairs_elsewhere\", \"environment_exposure\", \"incidents\",\n                  \"driving_pattern\", \"cleaning_maintenance\")\n\n#: The two categories promoted to their own hero quick-action tile (Oil &\n#: fluids, Battery & electrical) -- everything else in CATEGORY_ORDER renders\n#: as an \"Everything else\" row on the home screen. \"fuel\" is deliberately\n#: NOT removed here even though Fill-up is a quick action too: fill_up is\n#: only one of its three kinds (fuel_cap_issue/ran_low_or_out still need a\n#: way in), so the category stays reachable both ways.\n_QUICK_ACTION_CATEGORIES = (\"fluids\", \"battery_electrical\")\n\n#: hint -> (category, kind)|(category, None)|(None, None), the Snap & fill\n#: no-JS/no-vision fallback destination. Mirrors\n#: ``cuore.services.vision_bridge``'s own (private) hint -> suggested_kind\n#: table -- kept as a separate, small literal rather than reaching into that\n#: module's private attribute, same posture ``bench_routes._OUTCOMES``\n#: documents for why a small shared vocabulary sometimes isn't imported.\nSNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET: dict[str, tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str]]] = {\n    \"odometer\": (None, None),\n    \"fuel_pump\": (\"fuel\", \"fill_up\"),\n    \"oil_bottle\": (\"fluids\", None),\n    \"part_label\": (\"parts_repairs_elsewhere\", \"part_fitted_elsewhere\"),\n    \"receipt\": (\"fuel\", \"fill_up\"),\n    \"other\": (None, None),\n}\n\nSNAP_HINT_LABELS: dict[str, str] = {\n    \"odometer\": \"Odometer\", \"fuel_pump\": \"Fuel pump\", \"oil_bottle\": \"Oil bottle\",\n    \"part_label\": \"Part label\", \"receipt\": \"Receipt\", \"other\": \"Other\",\n}\n\n#: Query-string keys a Snap & fill redirect carries forward through the\n#: category -> kind picker chain, so a photo (and anything already read off\n#: it) survives even when the person still has to tap through to a specific\n#: kind by hand.\n_CARRY_KEYS = (\"media_id\", \"hint\", \"odometer_km\", \"source_odometer_km\")\n\n\ndef _page(request: Request, name: str, vin: str, active: str, **ctx: Any) -> HTMLResponse:\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, name, {\n        \"vin\": vin, \"active\": active, **ctx,\n    })\n\n\ndef _field(form: Any, name: str, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return str(form.get(name, default) or \"\").strip()\n\n\ndef _carry_qs(request: Request) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The subset of this request's query params worth forwarding through\n    the category -> kind picker chain (see :data:`_CARRY_KEYS`), already\n    URL-encoded and ``&``-joined -- \"\" when there is nothing to carry.\"\"\"\n    parts = []\n    for key in _CARRY_KEYS:\n        v = request.query_params.get(key)\n        if v:\n            parts.append(f\"{key}={quote(v)}\")\n    return \"&\".join(parts)\n\n\nasync def _upload_photo(vin: str, form: Any, *, caption: str) -> tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Reads the ``photo`` file field off an already-parsed form, if a real\n    file was chosen (same duck-typed guard ``media_routes.media_upload``\n    uses: ``request.form()`` returns a plain Starlette ``UploadFile``, not\n    FastAPI's subclass, so ``isinstance`` would miss every real upload).\n\n    Returns ``(media_id, error)`` -- exactly one is not ``None``. ``(None,\n    None)`` means no photo was offered at all, which is not an error on a\n    form where the camera tile is optional.\n    \"\"\"\n    photo = form.get(\"photo\")\n    if not (hasattr(photo, \"filename\") and hasattr(photo, \"read\") and photo.filename):\n        return None, None\n    body = await photo.read()\n    if not body:\n        return None, None\n    try:\n        row = media_store.add(vin, body, photo.filename, photo.content_type or \"image/jpeg\",\n                              target_kind=\"vehicle\", caption=caption, author=\"owner\")\n    except media_store.BadMedia as exc:\n        return None, str(exc)\n    return row.get(\"id\"), None\n\n\n# --- Home: the hero + quick actions ------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef home(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"Hero (name, odometer, one-line verdict), four quick actions (Fill-up\n    is the one red/primary tile -- the car's single most common report),\n    the unread-messages row, then \"Everything else\" for the remaining\n    categories. Plays the opening reveal on every visit (``show_intro``;\n    see ``m_base.html``'s own comment on why this is the only route that\n    passes it).\"\"\"\n    name = shop_bridge.resolve_vehicle_name(vin)\n    dossier = mes_bridge.workup(vin=vin)\n    identity = dossier.get(\"identity\") or {}\n    odo_last = identity.get(\"odometer_last_km\")\n    view = dossier_bridge.build_view(vin, dossier, None)\n    verdict = view.get(\"verdict\") or {}\n\n    try:\n        msgs = bridge.messages(vin)[\"messages\"]\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a feedback-store hiccup must not sink the home screen\n        msgs = []\n    unread = sum(1 for m in msgs if m.get(\"status\") == \"open\")\n\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    everything_else = [\n        {\"key\": k, \"label\": tax[k][\"label\"], \"kind_count\": len(tax[k][\"kinds\"])}\n        for k in CATEGORY_ORDER if k in tax and k not in _QUICK_ACTION_CATEGORIES\n    ]\n\n    quick_actions = [\n        {\"key\": \"fillup\", \"label\": \"Fill-up\", \"icon\": \"sys_fuel\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/fuel/fill_up\", \"primary\": True},\n        {\"key\": \"fluids\", \"label\": \"Oil & fluids\", \"icon\": \"sys_lubrication\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/fluids\", \"primary\": False},\n        {\"key\": \"battery\", \"label\": \"Battery & electrical\", \"icon\": \"sys_electrical_supply\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/battery_electrical\", \"primary\": False},\n        {\"key\": \"snap\", \"label\": \"Snap & fill\", \"icon\": \"camera\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/snap\", \"primary\": False},\n    ]\n\n    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params\n    return _page(request, \"m_home.html\", vin, \"add\", name=name, odo_last=odo_last,\n                verdict=verdict, quick_actions=quick_actions, unread=unread,\n                everything_else=everything_else, saved=saved, show_intro=True)\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef all_categories(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"Every category, one tile each -- the fallback destination for a Snap\n    & fill photo whose hint doesn't map to one category (odometer, other),\n    and a plain \"see everything\" page for anyone who wants it. Carries a\n    Snap-attached photo's query params forward onto each tile.\"\"\"\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    cats = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": tax[k][\"label\"], \"kind_count\": len(tax[k][\"kinds\"])}\n           for k in CATEGORY_ORDER if k in tax]\n    return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=cats,\n                carry=_carry_qs(request))\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef kinds_for_category(request: Request, vin: str, category: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    cat = tax.get(category)\n    if cat is None:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\",\n                     categories=[], carry=\"\", error=f\"unknown category {category!r}\")\n    kinds = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": kd[\"label\"], \"why_it_matters\": kd[\"why_it_matters\"]}\n            for k, kd in cat[\"kinds\"].items()]\n    return _page(request, \"m_kinds.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category,\n                category_label=cat[\"label\"], kinds=kinds, carry=_carry_qs(request))\n\n\ndef _last_fillup_fields(vin: str) -> dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"This car's most recently reported fill-up's field values, stringified\n    -- what the flagship fill-up form preselects/prefills so a repeat\n    fill-up with nothing changed needs no typing at all.\"\"\"\n    events = [e for e in store.load(vin)\n             if e.get(\"category\") == \"fuel\" and e.get(\"kind\") == \"fill_up\"]\n    if not events:\n        return {}\n    return {k: str(v) for k, v in (events[-1].get(\"fields\") or {}).items()}\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef add_form(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], carry=\"\",\n                     error=str(exc))\n    recents = {key: store.recent_values(vin, kind, key)\n               for key, spec in kd[\"fields\"].items() if spec.get(\"remember\")}\n\n    qp = request.query_params\n    media_id = qp.get(\"media_id\") or \"\"\n    prefill: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {}\n    for key in kd[\"fields\"]:\n        v = qp.get(key)\n        if v:\n            prefill[key] = {\"value\": v, \"source\": qp.get(f\"source_{key}\") or \"\"}\n\n    odometer_prefill = qp.get(\"odometer_km\") or \"\"\n    odometer_from_photo = qp.get(\"source_odometer_km\") == \"photo\"\n\n    if category == \"fuel\" and kind == \"fill_up\":\n        for k, v in _last_fillup_fields(vin).items():\n            prefill.setdefault(k, {\"value\": v, \"source\": \"\"})\n        return _page(request, \"m_fillup.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind,\n                    kd=kd, prefill=prefill, media_id=media_id,\n                    odometer_prefill=odometer_prefill, odometer_from_photo=odometer_from_photo)\n\n    return _page(request, \"m_form.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind, kd=kd,\n                recents=recents, prefill=prefill, media_id=media_id,\n                odometer_prefill=odometer_prefill, odometer_from_photo=odometer_from_photo)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def add_submit(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    form = await request.form()\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)\n\n    fields: dict[str, Any] = {}\n    fields_meta: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for key in kd[\"fields\"]:\n        spec = kd[\"fields\"][key]\n        if spec[\"type\"] == \"bool\":\n            fields[key] = _field(form, key) in (\"on\", \"true\", \"1\", \"yes\")\n        else:\n            v = _field(form, key)\n            if v:\n                fields[key] = v\n        if _field(form, f\"source_{key}\") == \"photo\":\n            fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"\n\n    at = _field(form, \"at\") or None\n    by_role = _field(form, \"by_role\") or \"owner\"\n    by_name = _field(form, \"by_name\")\n    note = _field(form, \"note\")\n    odo_raw = _field(form, \"odometer_km\")\n    odometer_km: Optional[float] = None\n    if odo_raw:\n        try:\n            odometer_km = float(odo_raw)\n        except ValueError:\n            return RedirectResponse(\n                url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error=odometer+must+be+a+number\",\n                status_code=303)\n\n    media_ids: list[str] = []\n    carried_media_id = _field(form, \"media_id\")\n    if carried_media_id:\n        media_ids.append(carried_media_id)\n\n    new_media_id, photo_error = await _upload_photo(\n        vin, form, caption=f\"owner report: {category}/{kind}\")\n    if photo_error:\n        return RedirectResponse(\n            url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error={quote('photo: ' + photo_error)}\",\n            status_code=303)\n    if new_media_id and new_media_id not in media_ids:\n        media_ids.append(new_media_id)\n\n    try:\n        rec = bridge.add(vin, category, kind, at=at, by_role=by_role, by_name=by_name,\n                         fields=fields, note=note, odometer_km=odometer_km,\n                         media_ids=media_ids, fields_meta=fields_meta)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(\n            url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)\n\n    return RedirectResponse(\n        url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{rec['id']}\", status_code=303)\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{id}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef add_confirm(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str, id: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"The full-screen \"record card\" after Save -- a thin-ruled summary of\n    exactly what was just stored, then \"Add another\" (same form, empty) or\n    \"Done\" (home). Reads the just-written row back rather than trusting the\n    POST body, so this always shows what is actually on disk.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], carry=\"\",\n                     error=str(exc))\n    event = next((e for e in store.load(vin, include_deleted=True) if e.get(\"id\") == id), None)\n    if event is None:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}\", status_code=303)\n\n    fields_meta = event.get(\"fields_meta\") or {}\n    fields_disp = []\n    for key, val in (event.get(\"fields\") or {}).items():\n        spec = kd[\"fields\"].get(key, {})\n        label = spec.get(\"label\") or key.replace(\"_\", \" \").title()\n        fields_disp.append({\n            \"label\": label, \"value\": val, \"unit\": spec.get(\"unit\", \"\"),\n            \"from_photo\": fields_meta.get(key) == \"photo\",\n        })\n\n    return _page(request, \"m_confirm.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind,\n                kd=kd, event=event, fields_disp=fields_disp)\n\n\n# --- Snap & fill --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/snap\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef snap_page(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    hints = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": SNAP_HINT_LABELS.get(k, k.title())}\n            for k in SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET]\n    return _page(request, \"m_snap.html\", vin, \"add\", hints=hints)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/snap\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def snap_submit(request: Request, vin: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"The no-JS (and no-vision-available) path: store the photo, then send\n    the person to the category/kind it's most likely about -- no field is\n    ever auto-filled here; only ``m.js``'s own client-side vision call does\n    that, and only when it actually has usable fields to offer.\"\"\"\n    form = await request.form()\n    hint = _field(form, \"hint\") or \"other\"\n    if hint not in SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET:\n        hint = \"other\"\n\n    media_id, error = await _upload_photo(vin, form, caption=f\"snap: {hint}\")\n    if error:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/snap?error={quote('photo: ' + error)}\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    if not media_id:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/snap?error=take+a+photo+first\", status_code=303)\n\n    category, kind = SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET.get(hint, (None, None))\n    qs = f\"media_id={quote(media_id)}&hint={quote(hint)}\"\n    if category and kind:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?{qs}\", status_code=303)\n    if category:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}?{qs}\", status_code=303)\n    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add?{qs}\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# --- Messages ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/messages\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef messages(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    data = bridge.messages(vin)\n    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params\n    return _page(request, \"m_messages.html\", vin, \"messages\",\n                messages=data[\"messages\"], saved=saved)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/messages/{id}/reply\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def reply(request: Request, vin: str, id: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    form = await request.form()\n    text = _field(form, \"text\")\n    by = _field(form, \"by\") or \"owner\"\n    if not text:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages?error=a+reply+is+required\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    try:\n        bridge.reply_message(id, text, by=by)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages?error={quote(str(exc))}\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages#saved\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# --- History --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/history\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef history(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    events = bridge.list_events(vin)[\"events\"]\n    events = sorted(events, key=lambda e: e.get(\"at\") or \"\", reverse=True)\n    rows = []\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    for e in events:\n        cat = tax.get(e.get(\"category\", \"\"), {})\n        kd = cat.get(\"kinds\", {}).get(e.get(\"kind\", \"\"), {})\n        rows.append({**e, \"category_label\": cat.get(\"label\", e.get(\"category\")),\n                    \"kind_label\": kd.get(\"label\", e.get(\"kind\"))})\n    return _page(request, \"m_history.html\", vin, \"history\", events=rows)\n\n\n# --- QR / LAN link ---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _lan_ip() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Best-guess LAN-reachable address for this machine. Never sends\n    traffic -- the UDP ``connect`` just picks the outbound route/interface\n    without a packet leaving for a reserved address.\"\"\"\n    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)\n    try:\n        s.connect((\"10.255.255.255\", 1))\n        return s.getsockname()[0]\n    except OSError:\n        return \"127.0.0.1\"\n    finally:\n        s.close()\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/qr\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef qr(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"A QR of the LAN URL for this page -- only rendered when the server is\n    actually bound to something other than loopback (``CUORE_HOST``, aka\n    the bind setting; see ``cuore/config.py`` and the handbook note this\n    satisfies). The ``qrcode`` package is not in this project's venv, and\n    writing a from-scratch QR matrix generator is out of scope for this\n    pass, so the LAN URL is rendered as selectable text instead -- the\n    fallback the brief explicitly allows.\n    \"\"\"\n    settings = settings_of(request)\n    if not settings.lan_exposed:\n        return _page(request, \"m_qr.html\", vin, \"add\", lan_url=None,\n                    reason=\"This server is only reachable from this machine \"\n                          \"(loopback). Set CUORE_HOST=0.0.0.0 in the keep-alive \"\n                          \"to serve the LAN -- see docs/handbook/\"\n                          \"05-methods-and-gotchas.md.\")\n    url = f\"http://{_lan_ip()}:{settings.port}/m/{vin}\"\n    return _page(request, \"m_qr.html\", vin, \"add\", lan_url=url, reason=None)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1552,"cache_read_input_tokens":215780,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1552,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TE9xGgCwUJduRHpgzYqVXf":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\owner_routes.py","content":"\"\"\"``/m/{vin}`` -- \"Tell CUORE\": the phone-first page where an owner, driver\nor mechanic records what the car cannot discover on its own, and reads\nmessages/questions from CUORE and the mechanic.\n\nRebuilt 2026-10-13 to the Ferrari-page benchmark the main app follows (see\n``cuore/web/static/cuore.css``'s \"Emphasis pass\" section) after the owner\nrejected the first pass as \"not up to the graphical and prestige standards\n... CUORE was built upon\". Still its own minimal layout (``templates/\nm_*.html``, own ``Jinja2Templates`` instance, no desktop tabs/hero, no\ndependency on ``cuore.web.routes``'s shared chrome) -- just a phone-width\npage with a bottom nav (Add / Messages / History), now hero-first with four\none-tap quick actions and a camera on every form.\n\n**Every record this page writes is ATTESTED, never a car measurement** --\nsee ``cuore/live/owner_events.py``'s docstring. The one-line footer on every\npage here says the same thing; do not remove it if these templates are\nedited later.\n\nWorks without JavaScript for everything except the \"Snap & fill\" photo\nauto-read: every form is a plain ``<form method=\"post\">`` (``enctype=\n\"multipart/form-data\"`` wherever a photo tile is present) that redirects on\nsuccess -- the camera tile, the fill-up flow and the Snap screen's own\n``Continue`` button all submit fine with scripting off; ``m.js`` only adds\nthe inline photo preview and the client-side call to\n``POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`` that can skip straight to a prefilled form.\nSame no-JS convention ``cuore.web.media_routes.media_upload`` and\n``inbox_routes`` use.\n\nPhoto contract with ``cuore.services.vision_bridge`` (built by another\nagent, now live as ``cuore.api.vision``): this module never calls it from\nPython -- only ``m.js`` does, client-side, against\n``POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`` (multipart ``file`` + ``hint``, one of\n:data:`SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET`'s keys). The response is\n``{provider, available, fields: {key: {value, confidence, unit}},\nsuggested_kind: \"category/kind\"|None, note}``. When it comes back usable,\n``m.js`` navigates straight to that kind's ``GET`` form with the read\nvalues and ``source_<key>=photo`` on the query string; :func:`add_form`\nturns those into the amber \"read from photo\" prefill, and\n:func:`add_submit` turns a submitted ``source_<key>=photo`` into\n``fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"`` on the stored event (the same provenance tag\nthe JSON API's ``POST /owner/{vin}/events`` body now also accepts, so a\nnative app can mark the same thing). When the endpoint is 404 (not wired\nup yet), unreachable, or answers ``available: false``, the **same** POST\n``/m/{vin}/snap`` this page already posts to without any JS at all is what\nthe person lands on -- there is no server-side dependency on vision ever\nsucceeding.\n\nRegistration note: ``cuore/app.py`` is owned by another agent. The one line\nneeded there, beside the other ``web`` routers::\n\n    app.include_router(owner_routes.router)\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport socket\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, RedirectResponse\nfrom fastapi.templating import Jinja2Templates\n\nfrom ..api.deps import require_token, settings_of\nfrom ..live import media as media_store\nfrom ..live import owner_events as store\nfrom ..services import dossier_bridge, mes_bridge, owner_events_bridge as bridge, shop_bridge\nfrom ..services.errors import BridgeError\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nTEMPLATE_DIR = HERE / \"templates\"\n\ntemplates = Jinja2Templates(directory=str(TEMPLATE_DIR))\n\nrouter = APIRouter(include_in_schema=False, dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n\n#: One pictogram-free label per category -- ``static/icons.svg`` has no\n#: symbol for any of these nine categories (its ``i-sys_*``/``i-symptom_*``\n#: set covers the systems graph and the driver symptom vocabulary, not\n#: owner-reported maintenance categories), so tiles render as plain labelled\n#: rows rather than inventing icons that would not match that file's house\n#: style. Flagged here rather than silently -- see the task note this\n#: satisfies.\nCATEGORY_ORDER = (\"fluids\", \"fuel\", \"battery_electrical\", \"tyres_wheels_brakes\",\n                  \"parts_repairs_elsewhere\", \"environment_exposure\", \"incidents\",\n                  \"driving_pattern\", \"cleaning_maintenance\")\n\n#: The two categories promoted to their own hero quick-action tile (Oil &\n#: fluids, Battery & electrical) -- everything else in CATEGORY_ORDER renders\n#: as an \"Everything else\" row on the home screen. \"fuel\" is deliberately\n#: NOT removed here even though Fill-up is a quick action too: fill_up is\n#: only one of its three kinds (fuel_cap_issue/ran_low_or_out still need a\n#: way in), so the category stays reachable both ways.\n_QUICK_ACTION_CATEGORIES = (\"fluids\", \"battery_electrical\")\n\n#: hint -> (category, kind)|(category, None)|(None, None), the Snap & fill\n#: no-JS/no-vision fallback destination. Mirrors\n#: ``cuore.services.vision_bridge``'s own (private) hint -> suggested_kind\n#: table -- kept as a separate, small literal rather than reaching into that\n#: module's private attribute, same posture ``bench_routes._OUTCOMES``\n#: documents for why a small shared vocabulary sometimes isn't imported.\nSNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET: dict[str, tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str]]] = {\n    \"odometer\": (None, None),\n    \"fuel_pump\": (\"fuel\", \"fill_up\"),\n    \"oil_bottle\": (\"fluids\", None),\n    \"part_label\": (\"parts_repairs_elsewhere\", \"part_fitted_elsewhere\"),\n    \"receipt\": (\"fuel\", \"fill_up\"),\n    \"other\": (None, None),\n}\n\nSNAP_HINT_LABELS: dict[str, str] = {\n    \"odometer\": \"Odometer\", \"fuel_pump\": \"Fuel pump\", \"oil_bottle\": \"Oil bottle\",\n    \"part_label\": \"Part label\", \"receipt\": \"Receipt\", \"other\": \"Other\",\n}\n\n#: Query-string keys a Snap & fill redirect carries forward through the\n#: category -> kind picker chain, so a photo (and anything already read off\n#: it) survives even when the person still has to tap through to a specific\n#: kind by hand.\n_CARRY_KEYS = (\"media_id\", \"hint\", \"odometer_km\", \"source_odometer_km\")\n\n\ndef _page(request: Request, name: str, vin: str, active: str, **ctx: Any) -> HTMLResponse:\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, name, {\n        \"vin\": vin, \"active\": active, **ctx,\n    })\n\n\ndef _field(form: Any, name: str, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return str(form.get(name, default) or \"\").strip()\n\n\ndef _carry_qs(request: Request) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The subset of this request's query params worth forwarding through\n    the category -> kind picker chain (see :data:`_CARRY_KEYS`), already\n    URL-encoded and ``&``-joined -- \"\" when there is nothing to carry.\"\"\"\n    parts = []\n    for key in _CARRY_KEYS:\n        v = request.query_params.get(key)\n        if v:\n            parts.append(f\"{key}={quote(v)}\")\n    return \"&\".join(parts)\n\n\nasync def _upload_photo(vin: str, form: Any, *, caption: str) -> tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Reads the ``photo`` file field off an already-parsed form, if a real\n    file was chosen (same duck-typed guard ``media_routes.media_upload``\n    uses: ``request.form()`` returns a plain Starlette ``UploadFile``, not\n    FastAPI's subclass, so ``isinstance`` would miss every real upload).\n\n    Returns ``(media_id, error)`` -- exactly one is not ``None``. ``(None,\n    None)`` means no photo was offered at all, which is not an error on a\n    form where the camera tile is optional.\n    \"\"\"\n    photo = form.get(\"photo\")\n    if not (hasattr(photo, \"filename\") and hasattr(photo, \"read\") and photo.filename):\n        return None, None\n    body = await photo.read()\n    if not body:\n        return None, None\n    try:\n        row = media_store.add(vin, body, photo.filename, photo.content_type or \"image/jpeg\",\n                              target_kind=\"vehicle\", caption=caption, author=\"owner\")\n    except media_store.BadMedia as exc:\n        return None, str(exc)\n    return row.get(\"id\"), None\n\n\n# --- Home: the hero + quick actions ------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef home(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"Hero (name, odometer, one-line verdict), four quick actions (Fill-up\n    is the one red/primary tile -- the car's single most common report),\n    the unread-messages row, then \"Everything else\" for the remaining\n    categories. Plays the opening reveal on every visit (``show_intro``;\n    see ``m_base.html``'s own comment on why this is the only route that\n    passes it).\"\"\"\n    name = shop_bridge.resolve_vehicle_name(vin)\n    dossier = mes_bridge.workup(vin=vin)\n    identity = dossier.get(\"identity\") or {}\n    odo_last = identity.get(\"odometer_last_km\")\n    view = dossier_bridge.build_view(vin, dossier, None)\n    verdict = view.get(\"verdict\") or {}\n\n    try:\n        msgs = bridge.messages(vin)[\"messages\"]\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a feedback-store hiccup must not sink the home screen\n        msgs = []\n    unread = sum(1 for m in msgs if m.get(\"status\") == \"open\")\n\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    everything_else = [\n        {\"key\": k, \"label\": tax[k][\"label\"], \"kind_count\": len(tax[k][\"kinds\"])}\n        for k in CATEGORY_ORDER if k in tax and k not in _QUICK_ACTION_CATEGORIES\n    ]\n\n    quick_actions = [\n        {\"key\": \"fillup\", \"label\": \"Fill-up\", \"icon\": \"sys_fuel\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/fuel/fill_up\", \"primary\": True},\n        {\"key\": \"fluids\", \"label\": \"Oil & fluids\", \"icon\": \"sys_lubrication\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/fluids\", \"primary\": False},\n        {\"key\": \"battery\", \"label\": \"Battery & electrical\", \"icon\": \"sys_electrical_supply\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/battery_electrical\", \"primary\": False},\n        {\"key\": \"snap\", \"label\": \"Snap & fill\", \"icon\": \"camera\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/snap\", \"primary\": False},\n    ]\n\n    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params\n    return _page(request, \"m_home.html\", vin, \"add\", name=name, odo_last=odo_last,\n                verdict=verdict, quick_actions=quick_actions, unread=unread,\n                everything_else=everything_else, saved=saved, show_intro=True)\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef all_categories(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"Every category, one tile each -- the fallback destination for a Snap\n    & fill photo whose hint doesn't map to one category (odometer, other),\n    and a plain \"see everything\" page for anyone who wants it. Carries a\n    Snap-attached photo's query params forward onto each tile.\"\"\"\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    cats = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": tax[k][\"label\"], \"kind_count\": len(tax[k][\"kinds\"])}\n           for k in CATEGORY_ORDER if k in tax]\n    return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=cats,\n                carry=_carry_qs(request))\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef kinds_for_category(request: Request, vin: str, category: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    cat = tax.get(category)\n    if cat is None:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\",\n                     categories=[], carry=\"\", error=f\"unknown category {category!r}\")\n    kinds = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": kd[\"label\"], \"why_it_matters\": kd[\"why_it_matters\"]}\n            for k, kd in cat[\"kinds\"].items()]\n    return _page(request, \"m_kinds.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category,\n                category_label=cat[\"label\"], kinds=kinds, carry=_carry_qs(request))\n\n\ndef _last_fillup_fields(vin: str) -> dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"This car's most recently reported fill-up's field values, stringified\n    -- what the flagship fill-up form preselects/prefills so a repeat\n    fill-up with nothing changed needs no typing at all.\"\"\"\n    events = [e for e in store.load(vin)\n             if e.get(\"category\") == \"fuel\" and e.get(\"kind\") == \"fill_up\"]\n    if not events:\n        return {}\n    return {k: str(v) for k, v in (events[-1].get(\"fields\") or {}).items()}\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef add_form(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], carry=\"\",\n                     error=str(exc))\n    recents = {key: store.recent_values(vin, kind, key)\n               for key, spec in kd[\"fields\"].items() if spec.get(\"remember\")}\n\n    qp = request.query_params\n    media_id = qp.get(\"media_id\") or \"\"\n    prefill: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {}\n    for key in kd[\"fields\"]:\n        v = qp.get(key)\n        if v:\n            prefill[key] = {\"value\": v, \"source\": qp.get(f\"source_{key}\") or \"\"}\n\n    odometer_prefill = qp.get(\"odometer_km\") or \"\"\n    odometer_from_photo = qp.get(\"source_odometer_km\") == \"photo\"\n\n    if category == \"fuel\" and kind == \"fill_up\":\n        for k, v in _last_fillup_fields(vin).items():\n            prefill.setdefault(k, {\"value\": v, \"source\": \"\"})\n        return _page(request, \"m_fillup.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind,\n                    kd=kd, prefill=prefill, media_id=media_id,\n                    odometer_prefill=odometer_prefill, odometer_from_photo=odometer_from_photo)\n\n    return _page(request, \"m_form.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind, kd=kd,\n                recents=recents, prefill=prefill, media_id=media_id,\n                odometer_prefill=odometer_prefill, odometer_from_photo=odometer_from_photo)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def add_submit(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    form = await request.form()\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)\n\n    fields: dict[str, Any] = {}\n    fields_meta: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for key in kd[\"fields\"]:\n        spec = kd[\"fields\"][key]\n        if spec[\"type\"] == \"bool\":\n            fields[key] = _field(form, key) in (\"on\", \"true\", \"1\", \"yes\")\n        else:\n            v = _field(form, key)\n            if v:\n                fields[key] = v\n        if _field(form, f\"source_{key}\") == \"photo\":\n            fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"\n\n    at = _field(form, \"at\") or None\n    by_role = _field(form, \"by_role\") or \"owner\"\n    by_name = _field(form, \"by_name\")\n    note = _field(form, \"note\")\n    odo_raw = _field(form, \"odometer_km\")\n    odometer_km: Optional[float] = None\n    if odo_raw:\n        try:\n            odometer_km = float(odo_raw)\n        except ValueError:\n            return RedirectResponse(\n                url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error=odometer+must+be+a+number\",\n                status_code=303)\n\n    media_ids: list[str] = []\n    carried_media_id = _field(form, \"media_id\")\n    if carried_media_id:\n        media_ids.append(carried_media_id)\n\n    new_media_id, photo_error = await _upload_photo(\n        vin, form, caption=f\"owner report: {category}/{kind}\")\n    if photo_error:\n        return RedirectResponse(\n            url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error={quote('photo: ' + photo_error)}\",\n            status_code=303)\n    if new_media_id and new_media_id not in media_ids:\n        media_ids.append(new_media_id)\n\n    try:\n        rec = bridge.add(vin, category, kind, at=at, by_role=by_role, by_name=by_name,\n                         fields=fields, note=note, odometer_km=odometer_km,\n                         media_ids=media_ids, fields_meta=fields_meta)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(\n            url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)\n\n    return RedirectResponse(\n        url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{rec['id']}\", status_code=303)\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{id}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef add_confirm(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str, id: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"The full-screen \"record card\" after Save -- a thin-ruled summary of\n    exactly what was just stored, then \"Add another\" (same form, empty) or\n    \"Done\" (home). Reads the just-written row back rather than trusting the\n    POST body, so this always shows what is actually on disk.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], carry=\"\",\n                     error=str(exc))\n    event = next((e for e in store.load(vin, include_deleted=True) if e.get(\"id\") == id), None)\n    if event is None:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}\", status_code=303)\n\n    fields_meta = event.get(\"fields_meta\") or {}\n    fields_disp = []\n    for key, val in (event.get(\"fields\") or {}).items():\n        spec = kd[\"fields\"].get(key, {})\n        label = spec.get(\"label\") or key.replace(\"_\", \" \").title()\n        fields_disp.append({\n            \"label\": label, \"value\": val, \"unit\": spec.get(\"unit\", \"\"),\n            \"from_photo\": fields_meta.get(key) == \"photo\",\n        })\n\n    return _page(request, \"m_confirm.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind,\n                kd=kd, event=event, fields_disp=fields_disp)\n\n\n# --- Snap & fill --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/snap\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef snap_page(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    hints = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": SNAP_HINT_LABELS.get(k, k.title())}\n            for k in SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET]\n    return _page(request, \"m_snap.html\", vin, \"add\", hints=hints)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/snap\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def snap_submit(request: Request, vin: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"The no-JS (and no-vision-available) path: store the photo, then send\n    the person to the category/kind it's most likely about -- no field is\n    ever auto-filled here; only ``m.js``'s own client-side vision call does\n    that, and only when it actually has usable fields to offer.\"\"\"\n    form = await request.form()\n    hint = _field(form, \"hint\") or \"other\"\n    if hint not in SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET:\n        hint = \"other\"\n\n    media_id, error = await _upload_photo(vin, form, caption=f\"snap: {hint}\")\n    if error:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/snap?error={quote('photo: ' + error)}\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    if not media_id:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/snap?error=take+a+photo+first\", status_code=303)\n\n    category, kind = SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET.get(hint, (None, None))\n    qs = f\"media_id={quote(media_id)}&hint={quote(hint)}\"\n    if category and kind:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?{qs}\", status_code=303)\n    if category:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}?{qs}\", status_code=303)\n    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add?{qs}\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# --- Messages ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/messages\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef messages(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    data = bridge.messages(vin)\n    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params\n    return _page(request, \"m_messages.html\", vin, \"messages\",\n                messages=data[\"messages\"], saved=saved)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/messages/{id}/reply\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def reply(request: Request, vin: str, id: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    form = await request.form()\n    text = _field(form, \"text\")\n    by = _field(form, \"by\") or \"owner\"\n    if not text:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages?error=a+reply+is+required\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    try:\n        bridge.reply_message(id, text, by=by)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages?error={quote(str(exc))}\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages#saved\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# --- History --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/history\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef history(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    events = bridge.list_events(vin)[\"events\"]\n    events = sorted(events, key=lambda e: e.get(\"at\") or \"\", reverse=True)\n    rows = []\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    for e in events:\n        cat = tax.get(e.get(\"category\", \"\"), {})\n        kd = cat.get(\"kinds\", {}).get(e.get(\"kind\", \"\"), {})\n        rows.append({**e, \"category_label\": cat.get(\"label\", e.get(\"category\")),\n                    \"kind_label\": kd.get(\"label\", e.get(\"kind\"))})\n    return _page(request, \"m_history.html\", vin, \"history\", events=rows)\n\n\n# --- QR / LAN link ---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _lan_ip() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Best-guess LAN-reachable address for this machine. Never sends\n    traffic -- the UDP ``connect`` just picks the outbound route/interface\n    without a packet leaving for a reserved address.\"\"\"\n    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)\n    try:\n        s.connect((\"10.255.255.255\", 1))\n        return s.getsockname()[0]\n    except OSError:\n        return \"127.0.0.1\"\n    finally:\n        s.close()\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/qr\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef qr(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"A QR of the LAN URL for this page -- only rendered when the server is\n    actually bound to something other than loopback (``CUORE_HOST``, aka\n    the bind setting; see ``cuore/config.py`` and the handbook note this\n    satisfies). The ``qrcode`` package is not in this project's venv, and\n    writing a from-scratch QR matrix generator is out of scope for this\n    pass, so the LAN URL is rendered as selectable text instead -- the\n    fallback the brief explicitly allows.\n    \"\"\"\n    settings = settings_of(request)\n    if not settings.lan_exposed:\n        return _page(request, \"m_qr.html\", vin, \"add\", lan_url=None,\n                    reason=\"This server is only reachable from this machine \"\n                          \"(loopback). Set CUORE_HOST=0.0.0.0 in the keep-alive \"\n                          \"to serve the LAN -- see docs/handbook/\"\n                          \"05-methods-and-gotchas.md.\")\n    url = f\"http://{_lan_ip()}:{settings.port}/m/{vin}\"\n    return _page(request, \"m_qr.html\", vin, \"add\", lan_url=url, reason=None)\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7e8d9abe-161f-4bde-bda4-77c024180239","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg14MXPcDe7hPbNRh9ZtY","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fe49c97-4b72-4acd-b823-311bb38ca308","timestamp":"2026-10-13T22:56:07.187Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"3fe49c97-4b72-4acd-b823-311bb38ca308","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1153797c-0a49-49a7-8dce-d1a3c6b99772","agentId":"a554eed87317d112b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TE9xGgCwUJduRHpgzYqVXf","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\owner_routes.py has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"88336825-fecb-4238-b87d-fbb45e0095c8","timestamp":"2026-10-13T22:56:07.567Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\owner_routes.py","content":"\"\"\"``/m/{vin}`` -- \"Tell CUORE\": the phone-first page where an owner, driver\nor mechanic records what the car cannot discover on its own, and reads\nmessages/questions from CUORE and the mechanic.\n\nRebuilt 2026-10-13 to the Ferrari-page benchmark the main app follows (see\n``cuore/web/static/cuore.css``'s \"Emphasis pass\" section) after the owner\nrejected the first pass as \"not up to the graphical and prestige standards\n... CUORE was built upon\". Still its own minimal layout (``templates/\nm_*.html``, own ``Jinja2Templates`` instance, no desktop tabs/hero, no\ndependency on ``cuore.web.routes``'s shared chrome) -- just a phone-width\npage with a bottom nav (Add / Messages / History), now hero-first with four\none-tap quick actions and a camera on every form.\n\n**Every record this page writes is ATTESTED, never a car measurement** --\nsee ``cuore/live/owner_events.py``'s docstring. The one-line footer on every\npage here says the same thing; do not remove it if these templates are\nedited later.\n\nWorks without JavaScript for everything except the \"Snap & fill\" photo\nauto-read: every form is a plain ``<form method=\"post\">`` (``enctype=\n\"multipart/form-data\"`` wherever a photo tile is present) that redirects on\nsuccess -- the camera tile, the fill-up flow and the Snap screen's own\n``Continue`` button all submit fine with scripting off; ``m.js`` only adds\nthe inline photo preview and the client-side call to\n``POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`` that can skip straight to a prefilled form.\nSame no-JS convention ``cuore.web.media_routes.media_upload`` and\n``inbox_routes`` use.\n\nPhoto contract with ``cuore.services.vision_bridge`` (built by another\nagent, now live as ``cuore.api.vision``): this module never calls it from\nPython -- only ``m.js`` does, client-side, against\n``POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`` (multipart ``file`` + ``hint``, one of\n:data:`SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET`'s keys). The response is\n``{provider, available, fields: {key: {value, confidence, unit}},\nsuggested_kind: \"category/kind\"|None, note}``. When it comes back usable,\n``m.js`` navigates straight to that kind's ``GET`` form with the read\nvalues and ``source_<key>=photo`` on the query string; :func:`add_form`\nturns those into the amber \"read from photo\" prefill, and\n:func:`add_submit` turns a submitted ``source_<key>=photo`` into\n``fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"`` on the stored event (the same provenance tag\nthe JSON API's ``POST /owner/{vin}/events`` body now also accepts, so a\nnative app can mark the same thing). When the endpoint is 404 (not wired\nup yet), unreachable, or answers ``available: false``, the **same** POST\n``/m/{vin}/snap`` this page already posts to without any JS at all is what\nthe person lands on -- there is no server-side dependency on vision ever\nsucceeding.\n\nRegistration note: ``cuore/app.py`` is owned by another agent. The one line\nneeded there, beside the other ``web`` routers::\n\n    app.include_router(owner_routes.router)\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport socket\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, RedirectResponse\nfrom fastapi.templating import Jinja2Templates\n\nfrom ..api.deps import require_token, settings_of\nfrom ..live import media as media_store\nfrom ..live import owner_events as store\nfrom ..services import dossier_bridge, mes_bridge, owner_events_bridge as bridge, shop_bridge\nfrom ..services.errors import BridgeError\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nTEMPLATE_DIR = HERE / \"templates\"\n\ntemplates = Jinja2Templates(directory=str(TEMPLATE_DIR))\n\nrouter = APIRouter(include_in_schema=False, dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n\n#: One pictogram-free label per category -- ``static/icons.svg`` has no\n#: symbol for any of these nine categories (its ``i-sys_*``/``i-symptom_*``\n#: set covers the systems graph and the driver symptom vocabulary, not\n#: owner-reported maintenance categories), so tiles render as plain labelled\n#: rows rather than inventing icons that would not match that file's house\n#: style. Flagged here rather than silently -- see the task note this\n#: satisfies.\nCATEGORY_ORDER = (\"fluids\", \"fuel\", \"battery_electrical\", \"tyres_wheels_brakes\",\n                  \"parts_repairs_elsewhere\", \"environment_exposure\", \"incidents\",\n                  \"driving_pattern\", \"cleaning_maintenance\")\n\n#: The two categories promoted to their own hero quick-action tile (Oil &\n#: fluids, Battery & electrical) -- everything else in CATEGORY_ORDER renders\n#: as an \"Everything else\" row on the home screen. \"fuel\" is deliberately\n#: NOT removed here even though Fill-up is a quick action too: fill_up is\n#: only one of its three kinds (fuel_cap_issue/ran_low_or_out still need a\n#: way in), so the category stays reachable both ways.\n_QUICK_ACTION_CATEGORIES = (\"fluids\", \"battery_electrical\")\n\n#: hint -> (category, kind)|(category, None)|(None, None), the Snap & fill\n#: no-JS/no-vision fallback destination. Mirrors\n#: ``cuore.services.vision_bridge``'s own (private) hint -> suggested_kind\n#: table -- kept as a separate, small literal rather than reaching into that\n#: module's private attribute, same posture ``bench_routes._OUTCOMES``\n#: documents for why a small shared vocabulary sometimes isn't imported.\nSNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET: dict[str, tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str]]] = {\n    \"odometer\": (None, None),\n    \"fuel_pump\": (\"fuel\", \"fill_up\"),\n    \"oil_bottle\": (\"fluids\", None),\n    \"part_label\": (\"parts_repairs_elsewhere\", \"part_fitted_elsewhere\"),\n    \"receipt\": (\"fuel\", \"fill_up\"),\n    \"other\": (None, None),\n}\n\nSNAP_HINT_LABELS: dict[str, str] = {\n    \"odometer\": \"Odometer\", \"fuel_pump\": \"Fuel pump\", \"oil_bottle\": \"Oil bottle\",\n    \"part_label\": \"Part label\", \"receipt\": \"Receipt\", \"other\": \"Other\",\n}\n\n#: Query-string keys a Snap & fill redirect carries forward through the\n#: category -> kind picker chain, so a photo (and anything already read off\n#: it) survives even when the person still has to tap through to a specific\n#: kind by hand.\n_CARRY_KEYS = (\"media_id\", \"hint\", \"odometer_km\", \"source_odometer_km\")\n\n\ndef _page(request: Request, name: str, vin: str, active: str, **ctx: Any) -> HTMLResponse:\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, name, {\n        \"vin\": vin, \"active\": active, **ctx,\n    })\n\n\ndef _field(form: Any, name: str, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return str(form.get(name, default) or \"\").strip()\n\n\ndef _carry_qs(request: Request) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The subset of this request's query params worth forwarding through\n    the category -> kind picker chain (see :data:`_CARRY_KEYS`), already\n    URL-encoded and ``&``-joined -- \"\" when there is nothing to carry.\"\"\"\n    parts = []\n    for key in _CARRY_KEYS:\n        v = request.query_params.get(key)\n        if v:\n            parts.append(f\"{key}={quote(v)}\")\n    return \"&\".join(parts)\n\n\nasync def _upload_photo(vin: str, form: Any, *, caption: str) -> tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Reads the ``photo`` file field off an already-parsed form, if a real\n    file was chosen (same duck-typed guard ``media_routes.media_upload``\n    uses: ``request.form()`` returns a plain Starlette ``UploadFile``, not\n    FastAPI's subclass, so ``isinstance`` would miss every real upload).\n\n    Returns ``(media_id, error)`` -- exactly one is not ``None``. ``(None,\n    None)`` means no photo was offered at all, which is not an error on a\n    form where the camera tile is optional.\n    \"\"\"\n    photo = form.get(\"photo\")\n    if not (hasattr(photo, \"filename\") and hasattr(photo, \"read\") and photo.filename):\n        return None, None\n    body = await photo.read()\n    if not body:\n        return None, None\n    try:\n        row = media_store.add(vin, body, photo.filename, photo.content_type or \"image/jpeg\",\n                              target_kind=\"vehicle\", caption=caption, author=\"owner\")\n    except media_store.BadMedia as exc:\n        return None, str(exc)\n    return row.get(\"id\"), None\n\n\n# --- Home: the hero + quick actions ------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef home(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"Hero (name, odometer, one-line verdict), four quick actions (Fill-up\n    is the one red/primary tile -- the car's single most common report),\n    the unread-messages row, then \"Everything else\" for the remaining\n    categories. Plays the opening reveal on every visit (``show_intro``;\n    see ``m_base.html``'s own comment on why this is the only route that\n    passes it).\"\"\"\n    name = shop_bridge.resolve_vehicle_name(vin)\n    dossier = mes_bridge.workup(vin=vin)\n    identity = dossier.get(\"identity\") or {}\n    odo_last = identity.get(\"odometer_last_km\")\n    view = dossier_bridge.build_view(vin, dossier, None)\n    verdict = view.get(\"verdict\") or {}\n\n    try:\n        msgs = bridge.messages(vin)[\"messages\"]\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a feedback-store hiccup must not sink the home screen\n        msgs = []\n    unread = sum(1 for m in msgs if m.get(\"status\") == \"open\")\n\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    everything_else = [\n        {\"key\": k, \"label\": tax[k][\"label\"], \"kind_count\": len(tax[k][\"kinds\"])}\n        for k in CATEGORY_ORDER if k in tax and k not in _QUICK_ACTION_CATEGORIES\n    ]\n\n    quick_actions = [\n        {\"key\": \"fillup\", \"label\": \"Fill-up\", \"icon\": \"sys_fuel\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/fuel/fill_up\", \"primary\": True},\n        {\"key\": \"fluids\", \"label\": \"Oil & fluids\", \"icon\": \"sys_lubrication\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/fluids\", \"primary\": False},\n        {\"key\": \"battery\", \"label\": \"Battery & electrical\", \"icon\": \"sys_electrical_supply\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/battery_electrical\", \"primary\": False},\n        {\"key\": \"snap\", \"label\": \"Snap & fill\", \"icon\": \"camera\",\n         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/snap\", \"primary\": False},\n    ]\n\n    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params\n    return _page(request, \"m_home.html\", vin, \"add\", name=name, odo_last=odo_last,\n                verdict=verdict, quick_actions=quick_actions, unread=unread,\n                everything_else=everything_else, saved=saved, show_intro=True)\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef all_categories(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"Every category, one tile each -- the fallback destination for a Snap\n    & fill photo whose hint doesn't map to one category (odometer, other),\n    and a plain \"see everything\" page for anyone who wants it. Carries a\n    Snap-attached photo's query params forward onto each tile.\"\"\"\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    cats = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": tax[k][\"label\"], \"kind_count\": len(tax[k][\"kinds\"])}\n           for k in CATEGORY_ORDER if k in tax]\n    return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=cats,\n                carry=_carry_qs(request))\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef kinds_for_category(request: Request, vin: str, category: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    cat = tax.get(category)\n    if cat is None:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\",\n                     categories=[], carry=\"\", error=f\"unknown category {category!r}\")\n    kinds = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": kd[\"label\"], \"why_it_matters\": kd[\"why_it_matters\"]}\n            for k, kd in cat[\"kinds\"].items()]\n    return _page(request, \"m_kinds.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category,\n                category_label=cat[\"label\"], kinds=kinds, carry=_carry_qs(request))\n\n\ndef _last_fillup_fields(vin: str) -> dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"This car's most recently reported fill-up's field values, stringified\n    -- what the flagship fill-up form preselects/prefills so a repeat\n    fill-up with nothing changed needs no typing at all.\"\"\"\n    events = [e for e in store.load(vin)\n             if e.get(\"category\") == \"fuel\" and e.get(\"kind\") == \"fill_up\"]\n    if not events:\n        return {}\n    return {k: str(v) for k, v in (events[-1].get(\"fields\") or {}).items()}\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef add_form(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], carry=\"\",\n                     error=str(exc))\n    recents = {key: store.recent_values(vin, kind, key)\n               for key, spec in kd[\"fields\"].items() if spec.get(\"remember\")}\n\n    qp = request.query_params\n    media_id = qp.get(\"media_id\") or \"\"\n    prefill: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {}\n    for key in kd[\"fields\"]:\n        v = qp.get(key)\n        if v:\n            prefill[key] = {\"value\": v, \"source\": qp.get(f\"source_{key}\") or \"\"}\n\n    odometer_prefill = qp.get(\"odometer_km\") or \"\"\n    odometer_from_photo = qp.get(\"source_odometer_km\") == \"photo\"\n\n    if category == \"fuel\" and kind == \"fill_up\":\n        for k, v in _last_fillup_fields(vin).items():\n            prefill.setdefault(k, {\"value\": v, \"source\": \"\"})\n        return _page(request, \"m_fillup.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind,\n                    kd=kd, prefill=prefill, media_id=media_id,\n                    odometer_prefill=odometer_prefill, odometer_from_photo=odometer_from_photo)\n\n    return _page(request, \"m_form.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind, kd=kd,\n                recents=recents, prefill=prefill, media_id=media_id,\n                odometer_prefill=odometer_prefill, odometer_from_photo=odometer_from_photo)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def add_submit(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    form = await request.form()\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)\n\n    fields: dict[str, Any] = {}\n    fields_meta: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for key in kd[\"fields\"]:\n        spec = kd[\"fields\"][key]\n        if spec[\"type\"] == \"bool\":\n            fields[key] = _field(form, key) in (\"on\", \"true\", \"1\", \"yes\")\n        else:\n            v = _field(form, key)\n            if v:\n                fields[key] = v\n        if _field(form, f\"source_{key}\") == \"photo\":\n            fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"\n\n    at = _field(form, \"at\") or None\n    by_role = _field(form, \"by_role\") or \"owner\"\n    by_name = _field(form, \"by_name\")\n    note = _field(form, \"note\")\n    odo_raw = _field(form, \"odometer_km\")\n    odometer_km: Optional[float] = None\n    if odo_raw:\n        try:\n            odometer_km = float(odo_raw)\n        except ValueError:\n            return RedirectResponse(\n                url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error=odometer+must+be+a+number\",\n                status_code=303)\n\n    media_ids: list[str] = []\n    carried_media_id = _field(form, \"media_id\")\n    if carried_media_id:\n        media_ids.append(carried_media_id)\n\n    new_media_id, photo_error = await _upload_photo(\n        vin, form, caption=f\"owner report: {category}/{kind}\")\n    if photo_error:\n        return RedirectResponse(\n            url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error={quote('photo: ' + photo_error)}\",\n            status_code=303)\n    if new_media_id and new_media_id not in media_ids:\n        media_ids.append(new_media_id)\n\n    try:\n        rec = bridge.add(vin, category, kind, at=at, by_role=by_role, by_name=by_name,\n                         fields=fields, note=note, odometer_km=odometer_km,\n                         media_ids=media_ids, fields_meta=fields_meta)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(\n            url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)\n\n    return RedirectResponse(\n        url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{rec['id']}\", status_code=303)\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{id}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef add_confirm(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str, id: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"The full-screen \"record card\" after Save -- a thin-ruled summary of\n    exactly what was just stored, then \"Add another\" (same form, empty) or\n    \"Done\" (home). Reads the just-written row back rather than trusting the\n    POST body, so this always shows what is actually on disk.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], carry=\"\",\n                     error=str(exc))\n    event = next((e for e in store.load(vin, include_deleted=True) if e.get(\"id\") == id), None)\n    if event is None:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}\", status_code=303)\n\n    fields_meta = event.get(\"fields_meta\") or {}\n    fields_disp = []\n    for key, val in (event.get(\"fields\") or {}).items():\n        spec = kd[\"fields\"].get(key, {})\n        label = spec.get(\"label\") or key.replace(\"_\", \" \").title()\n        fields_disp.append({\n            \"label\": label, \"value\": val, \"unit\": spec.get(\"unit\", \"\"),\n            \"from_photo\": fields_meta.get(key) == \"photo\",\n        })\n\n    return _page(request, \"m_confirm.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind,\n                kd=kd, event=event, fields_disp=fields_disp)\n\n\n# --- Snap & fill --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/snap\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef snap_page(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    hints = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": SNAP_HINT_LABELS.get(k, k.title())}\n            for k in SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET]\n    return _page(request, \"m_snap.html\", vin, \"add\", hints=hints)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/snap\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def snap_submit(request: Request, vin: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    \"\"\"The no-JS (and no-vision-available) path: store the photo, then send\n    the person to the category/kind it's most likely about -- no field is\n    ever auto-filled here; only ``m.js``'s own client-side vision call does\n    that, and only when it actually has usable fields to offer.\"\"\"\n    form = await request.form()\n    hint = _field(form, \"hint\") or \"other\"\n    if hint not in SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET:\n        hint = \"other\"\n\n    media_id, error = await _upload_photo(vin, form, caption=f\"snap: {hint}\")\n    if error:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/snap?error={quote('photo: ' + error)}\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    if not media_id:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/snap?error=take+a+photo+first\", status_code=303)\n\n    category, kind = SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET.get(hint, (None, None))\n    qs = f\"media_id={quote(media_id)}&hint={quote(hint)}\"\n    if category and kind:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?{qs}\", status_code=303)\n    if category:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}?{qs}\", status_code=303)\n    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add?{qs}\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# --- Messages ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/messages\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef messages(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    data = bridge.messages(vin)\n    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params\n    return _page(request, \"m_messages.html\", vin, \"messages\",\n                messages=data[\"messages\"], saved=saved)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/messages/{id}/reply\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def reply(request: Request, vin: str, id: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    form = await request.form()\n    text = _field(form, \"text\")\n    by = _field(form, \"by\") or \"owner\"\n    if not text:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages?error=a+reply+is+required\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    try:\n        bridge.reply_message(id, text, by=by)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages?error={quote(str(exc))}\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages#saved\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# --- History --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/history\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef history(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    events = bridge.list_events(vin)[\"events\"]\n    events = sorted(events, key=lambda e: e.get(\"at\") or \"\", reverse=True)\n    rows = []\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    for e in events:\n        cat = tax.get(e.get(\"category\", \"\"), {})\n        kd = cat.get(\"kinds\", {}).get(e.get(\"kind\", \"\"), {})\n        rows.append({**e, \"category_label\": cat.get(\"label\", e.get(\"category\")),\n                    \"kind_label\": kd.get(\"label\", e.get(\"kind\"))})\n    return _page(request, \"m_history.html\", vin, \"history\", events=rows)\n\n\n# --- QR / LAN link ---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _lan_ip() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Best-guess LAN-reachable address for this machine. Never sends\n    traffic -- the UDP ``connect`` just picks the outbound route/interface\n    without a packet leaving for a reserved address.\"\"\"\n    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)\n    try:\n        s.connect((\"10.255.255.255\", 1))\n        return s.getsockname()[0]\n    except OSError:\n        return \"127.0.0.1\"\n    finally:\n        s.close()\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/qr\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef qr(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"A QR of the LAN URL for this page -- only rendered when the server is\n    actually bound to something other than loopback (``CUORE_HOST``, aka\n    the bind setting; see ``cuore/config.py`` and the handbook note this\n    satisfies). The ``qrcode`` package is not in this project's venv, and\n    writing a from-scratch QR matrix generator is out of scope for this\n    pass, so the LAN URL is rendered as selectable text instead -- the\n    fallback the brief explicitly allows.\n    \"\"\"\n    settings = settings_of(request)\n    if not settings.lan_exposed:\n        return _page(request, \"m_qr.html\", vin, \"add\", lan_url=None,\n                    reason=\"This server is only reachable from this machine \"\n                          \"(loopback). Set CUORE_HOST=0.0.0.0 in the keep-alive \"\n                          \"to serve the LAN -- see docs/handbook/\"\n                          \"05-methods-and-gotchas.md.\")\n    url = f\"http://{_lan_ip()}:{settings.port}/m/{vin}\"\n    return _page(request, \"m_qr.html\", vin, \"add\", lan_url=url, reason=None)\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":21,"newStart":2,"newLines":49,"lines":[" or mechanic records what the car cannot discover on its own, and reads"," messages/questions from CUORE and the mechanic."," ","-Deliberately its own minimal layout (``templates/m_*.html``, own","-``Jinja2Templates`` instance), same \"built concurrently with other agents\"","-posture as ``cuore.web.media_routes``/``timeline_routes``: no desktop","-tabs/hero, no dependency on ``cuore.web.routes``'s shared chrome, just a","-phone-width page with a bottom nav (Add / Messages / History).","+Rebuilt 2026-10-13 to the Ferrari-page benchmark the main app follows (see","+``cuore/web/static/cuore.css``'s \"Emphasis pass\" section) after the owner","+rejected the first pass as \"not up to the graphical and prestige standards","+... CUORE was built upon\". Still its own minimal layout (``templates/","+m_*.html``, own ``Jinja2Templates`` instance, no desktop tabs/hero, no","+dependency on ``cuore.web.routes``'s shared chrome) -- just a phone-width","+page with a bottom nav (Add / Messages / History), now hero-first with four","+one-tap quick actions and a camera on every form."," "," **Every record this page writes is ATTESTED, never a car measurement** --"," see ``cuore/live/owner_events.py``'s docstring. The one-line footer on every"," page here says the same thing; do not remove it if these templates are"," edited later."," ","-Works without JavaScript: every form is a plain ``<form method=\"post\">``","-that redirects back to ``/m/{vin}#saved`` on success, same no-JS convention","-``cuore.web.media_routes.media_upload`` and ``inbox_routes`` use.","+Works without JavaScript for everything except the \"Snap & fill\" photo","+auto-read: every form is a plain ``<form method=\"post\">`` (``enctype=","+\"multipart/form-data\"`` wherever a photo tile is present) that redirects on","+success -- the camera tile, the fill-up flow and the Snap screen's own","+``Continue`` button all submit fine with scripting off; ``m.js`` only adds","+the inline photo preview and the client-side call to","+``POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`` that can skip straight to a prefilled form.","+Same no-JS convention ``cuore.web.media_routes.media_upload`` and","+``inbox_routes`` use."," ","+Photo contract with ``cuore.services.vision_bridge`` (built by another","+agent, now live as ``cuore.api.vision``): this module never calls it from","+Python -- only ``m.js`` does, client-side, against","+``POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`` (multipart ``file`` + ``hint``, one of","+:data:`SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET`'s keys). The response is","+``{provider, available, fields: {key: {value, confidence, unit}},","+suggested_kind: \"category/kind\"|None, note}``. When it comes back usable,","+``m.js`` navigates straight to that kind's ``GET`` form with the read","+values and ``source_<key>=photo`` on the query string; :func:`add_form`","+turns those into the amber \"read from photo\" prefill, and","+:func:`add_submit` turns a submitted ``source_<key>=photo`` into","+``fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"`` on the stored event (the same provenance tag","+the JSON API's ``POST /owner/{vin}/events`` body now also accepts, so a","+native app can mark the same thing). When the endpoint is 404 (not wired","+up yet), unreachable, or answers ``available: false``, the **same** POST","+``/m/{vin}/snap`` this page already posts to without any JS at all is what","+the person lands on -- there is no server-side dependency on vision ever","+succeeding.","+"," Registration note: ``cuore/app.py`` is owned by another agent. The one line"," needed there, beside the other ``web`` routers::"," "]},{"oldStart":35,"oldLines":8,"newStart":63,"newLines":9,"lines":[" from fastapi.templating import Jinja2Templates"," "," from ..api.deps import require_token, settings_of","+from ..live import media as media_store"," from ..live import owner_events as store","-from ..services import owner_events_bridge as bridge","+from ..services import dossier_bridge, mes_bridge, owner_events_bridge as bridge, shop_bridge"," from ..services.errors import BridgeError"," "," HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent"]},{"oldStart":50,"oldLines":14,"newStart":79,"newLines":48,"lines":[" #: symbol for any of these nine categories (its ``i-sys_*``/``i-symptom_*``"," #: set covers the systems graph and the driver symptom vocabulary, not"," #: owner-reported maintenance categories), so tiles render as plain labelled","-#: cards rather than inventing icons that would not match that file's house","+#: rows rather than inventing icons that would not match that file's house"," #: style. Flagged here rather than silently -- see the task note this"," #: satisfies."," CATEGORY_ORDER = (\"fluids\", \"fuel\", \"battery_electrical\", \"tyres_wheels_brakes\",","                   \"parts_repairs_elsewhere\", \"environment_exposure\", \"incidents\",","                   \"driving_pattern\", \"cleaning_maintenance\")"," ","+#: The two categories promoted to their own hero quick-action tile (Oil &","+#: fluids, Battery & electrical) -- everything else in CATEGORY_ORDER renders","+#: as an \"Everything else\" row on the home screen. \"fuel\" is deliberately","+#: NOT removed here even though Fill-up is a quick action too: fill_up is","+#: only one of its three kinds (fuel_cap_issue/ran_low_or_out still need a","+#: way in), so the category stays reachable both ways.","+_QUICK_ACTION_CATEGORIES = (\"fluids\", \"battery_electrical\")"," ","+#: hint -> (category, kind)|(category, None)|(None, None), the Snap & fill","+#: no-JS/no-vision fallback destination. Mirrors","+#: ``cuore.services.vision_bridge``'s own (private) hint -> suggested_kind","+#: table -- kept as a separate, small literal rather than reaching into that","+#: module's private attribute, same posture ``bench_routes._OUTCOMES``","+#: documents for why a small shared vocabulary sometimes isn't imported.","+SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET: dict[str, tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str]]] = {","+    \"odometer\": (None, None),","+    \"fuel_pump\": (\"fuel\", \"fill_up\"),","+    \"oil_bottle\": (\"fluids\", None),","+    \"part_label\": (\"parts_repairs_elsewhere\", \"part_fitted_elsewhere\"),","+    \"receipt\": (\"fuel\", \"fill_up\"),","+    \"other\": (None, None),","+}","+","+SNAP_HINT_LABELS: dict[str, str] = {","+    \"odometer\": \"Odometer\", \"fuel_pump\": \"Fuel pump\", \"oil_bottle\": \"Oil bottle\",","+    \"part_label\": \"Part label\", \"receipt\": \"Receipt\", \"other\": \"Other\",","+}","+","+#: Query-string keys a Snap & fill redirect carries forward through the","+#: category -> kind picker chain, so a photo (and anything already read off","+#: it) survives even when the person still has to tap through to a specific","+#: kind by hand.","+_CARRY_KEYS = (\"media_id\", \"hint\", \"odometer_km\", \"source_odometer_km\")","+","+"," def _page(request: Request, name: str, vin: str, active: str, **ctx: Any) -> HTMLResponse:","     return templates.TemplateResponse(request, name, {","         \"vin\": vin, \"active\": active, **ctx,"]},{"oldStart":68,"oldLines":17,"newStart":131,"newLines":100,"lines":["     return str(form.get(name, default) or \"\").strip()"," "," ","-# --- Add: category -> kind -> one-screen form --------------------------------","+def _carry_qs(request: Request) -> str:","+    \"\"\"The subset of this request's query params worth forwarding through","+    the category -> kind picker chain (see :data:`_CARRY_KEYS`), already","+    URL-encoded and ``&``-joined -- \"\" when there is nothing to carry.\"\"\"","+    parts = []","+    for key in _CARRY_KEYS:","+        v = request.query_params.get(key)","+        if v:","+            parts.append(f\"{key}={quote(v)}\")","+    return \"&\".join(parts)"," "," ","+async def _upload_photo(vin: str, form: Any, *, caption: str) -> tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str]]:","+    \"\"\"Reads the ``photo`` file field off an already-parsed form, if a real","+    file was chosen (same duck-typed guard ``media_routes.media_upload``","+    uses: ``request.form()`` returns a plain Starlette ``UploadFile``, not","+    FastAPI's subclass, so ``isinstance`` would miss every real upload).","+","+    Returns ``(media_id, error)`` -- exactly one is not ``None``. ``(None,","+    None)`` means no photo was offered at all, which is not an error on a","+    form where the camera tile is optional.","+    \"\"\"","+    photo = form.get(\"photo\")","+    if not (hasattr(photo, \"filename\") and hasattr(photo, \"read\") and photo.filename):","+        return None, None","+    body = await photo.read()","+    if not body:","+        return None, None","+    try:","+        row = media_store.add(vin, body, photo.filename, photo.content_type or \"image/jpeg\",","+                              target_kind=\"vehicle\", caption=caption, author=\"owner\")","+    except media_store.BadMedia as exc:","+        return None, str(exc)","+    return row.get(\"id\"), None","+","+","+# --- Home: the hero + quick actions ------------------------------------------","+","+"," @router.get(\"/m/{vin}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)"," def home(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:","-    \"\"\"Category tiles -- the landing/Add screen.\"\"\"","+    \"\"\"Hero (name, odometer, one-line verdict), four quick actions (Fill-up","+    is the one red/primary tile -- the car's single most common report),","+    the unread-messages row, then \"Everything else\" for the remaining","+    categories. Plays the opening reveal on every visit (``show_intro``;","+    see ``m_base.html``'s own comment on why this is the only route that","+    passes it).\"\"\"","+    name = shop_bridge.resolve_vehicle_name(vin)","+    dossier = mes_bridge.workup(vin=vin)","+    identity = dossier.get(\"identity\") or {}","+    odo_last = identity.get(\"odometer_last_km\")","+    view = dossier_bridge.build_view(vin, dossier, None)","+    verdict = view.get(\"verdict\") or {}","+","+    try:","+        msgs = bridge.messages(vin)[\"messages\"]","+    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a feedback-store hiccup must not sink the home screen","+        msgs = []","+    unread = sum(1 for m in msgs if m.get(\"status\") == \"open\")","+","     tax = store.TAXONOMY","+    everything_else = [","+        {\"key\": k, \"label\": tax[k][\"label\"], \"kind_count\": len(tax[k][\"kinds\"])}","+        for k in CATEGORY_ORDER if k in tax and k not in _QUICK_ACTION_CATEGORIES","+    ]","+","+    quick_actions = [","+        {\"key\": \"fillup\", \"label\": \"Fill-up\", \"icon\": \"sys_fuel\",","+         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/fuel/fill_up\", \"primary\": True},","+        {\"key\": \"fluids\", \"label\": \"Oil & fluids\", \"icon\": \"sys_lubrication\",","+         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/fluids\", \"primary\": False},","+        {\"key\": \"battery\", \"label\": \"Battery & electrical\", \"icon\": \"sys_electrical_supply\",","+         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/add/battery_electrical\", \"primary\": False},","+        {\"key\": \"snap\", \"label\": \"Snap & fill\", \"icon\": \"camera\",","+         \"href\": f\"/m/{vin}/snap\", \"primary\": False},","+    ]","+","+    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params","+    return _page(request, \"m_home.html\", vin, \"add\", name=name, odo_last=odo_last,","+                verdict=verdict, quick_actions=quick_actions, unread=unread,","+                everything_else=everything_else, saved=saved, show_intro=True)","+","+","+@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add\", response_class=HTMLResponse)","+def all_categories(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:","+    \"\"\"Every category, one tile each -- the fallback destination for a Snap","+    & fill photo whose hint doesn't map to one category (odometer, other),","+    and a plain \"see everything\" page for anyone who wants it. Carries a","+    Snap-attached photo's query params forward onto each tile.\"\"\"","+    tax = store.TAXONOMY","     cats = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": tax[k][\"label\"], \"kind_count\": len(tax[k][\"kinds\"])}","            for k in CATEGORY_ORDER if k in tax]","-    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params","-    return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=cats, saved=saved)","+    return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=cats,","+                carry=_carry_qs(request))"," "," "," @router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)"]},{"oldStart":87,"oldLines":23,"newStart":233,"newLines":55,"lines":["     cat = tax.get(category)","     if cat is None:","         return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\",","-                     categories=[], error=f\"unknown category {category!r}\")","+                     categories=[], carry=\"\", error=f\"unknown category {category!r}\")","     kinds = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": kd[\"label\"], \"why_it_matters\": kd[\"why_it_matters\"]}","             for k, kd in cat[\"kinds\"].items()]","     return _page(request, \"m_kinds.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category,","-                category_label=cat[\"label\"], kinds=kinds)","+                category_label=cat[\"label\"], kinds=kinds, carry=_carry_qs(request))"," "," ","+def _last_fillup_fields(vin: str) -> dict[str, str]:","+    \"\"\"This car's most recently reported fill-up's field values, stringified","+    -- what the flagship fill-up form preselects/prefills so a repeat","+    fill-up with nothing changed needs no typing at all.\"\"\"","+    events = [e for e in store.load(vin)","+             if e.get(\"category\") == \"fuel\" and e.get(\"kind\") == \"fill_up\"]","+    if not events:","+        return {}","+    return {k: str(v) for k, v in (events[-1].get(\"fields\") or {}).items()}","+","+"," @router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)"," def add_form(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str) -> HTMLResponse:","     try:","         kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)","     except ValueError as exc:","-        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], error=str(exc))","+        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], carry=\"\",","+                     error=str(exc))","     recents = {key: store.recent_values(vin, kind, key)","                for key, spec in kd[\"fields\"].items() if spec.get(\"remember\")}","+","+    qp = request.query_params","+    media_id = qp.get(\"media_id\") or \"\"","+    prefill: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {}","+    for key in kd[\"fields\"]:","+        v = qp.get(key)","+        if v:","+            prefill[key] = {\"value\": v, \"source\": qp.get(f\"source_{key}\") or \"\"}","+","+    odometer_prefill = qp.get(\"odometer_km\") or \"\"","+    odometer_from_photo = qp.get(\"source_odometer_km\") == \"photo\"","+","+    if category == \"fuel\" and kind == \"fill_up\":","+        for k, v in _last_fillup_fields(vin).items():","+            prefill.setdefault(k, {\"value\": v, \"source\": \"\"})","+        return _page(request, \"m_fillup.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind,","+                    kd=kd, prefill=prefill, media_id=media_id,","+                    odometer_prefill=odometer_prefill, odometer_from_photo=odometer_from_photo)","+","     return _page(request, \"m_form.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind, kd=kd,","-                 recents=recents)","+                recents=recents, prefill=prefill, media_id=media_id,","+                odometer_prefill=odometer_prefill, odometer_from_photo=odometer_from_photo)"," "," "," @router.post(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)"]},{"oldStart":115,"oldLines":6,"newStart":293,"newLines":7,"lines":["         return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)"," ","     fields: dict[str, Any] = {}","+    fields_meta: dict[str, str] = {}","     for key in kd[\"fields\"]:","         spec = kd[\"fields\"][key]","         if spec[\"type\"] == \"bool\":"]},{"oldStart":123,"oldLines":6,"newStart":302,"newLines":8,"lines":["             v = _field(form, key)","             if v:","                 fields[key] = v","+        if _field(form, f\"source_{key}\") == \"photo\":","+            fields_meta[key] = \"photo\""," ","     at = _field(form, \"at\") or None","     by_role = _field(form, \"by_role\") or \"owner\""]},{"oldStart":138,"oldLines":16,"newStart":319,"newLines":98,"lines":["                 url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error=odometer+must+be+a+number\",","                 status_code=303)"," ","+    media_ids: list[str] = []","+    carried_media_id = _field(form, \"media_id\")","+    if carried_media_id:","+        media_ids.append(carried_media_id)","+","+    new_media_id, photo_error = await _upload_photo(","+        vin, form, caption=f\"owner report: {category}/{kind}\")","+    if photo_error:","+        return RedirectResponse(","+            url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error={quote('photo: ' + photo_error)}\",","+            status_code=303)","+    if new_media_id and new_media_id not in media_ids:","+        media_ids.append(new_media_id)","+","     try:","-        bridge.add(vin, category, kind, at=at, by_role=by_role, by_name=by_name,","-                  fields=fields, note=note, odometer_km=odometer_km)","+        rec = bridge.add(vin, category, kind, at=at, by_role=by_role, by_name=by_name,","+                         fields=fields, note=note, odometer_km=odometer_km,","+                         media_ids=media_ids, fields_meta=fields_meta)","     except BridgeError as exc:","         return RedirectResponse(","             url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)"," ","-    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}#saved\", status_code=303)","+    return RedirectResponse(","+        url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{rec['id']}\", status_code=303)"," "," ","+@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}/confirm/{id}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)","+def add_confirm(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str, id: str) -> HTMLResponse:","+    \"\"\"The full-screen \"record card\" after Save -- a thin-ruled summary of","+    exactly what was just stored, then \"Add another\" (same form, empty) or","+    \"Done\" (home). Reads the just-written row back rather than trusting the","+    POST body, so this always shows what is actually on disk.\"\"\"","+    try:","+        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)","+    except ValueError as exc:","+        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], carry=\"\",","+                     error=str(exc))","+    event = next((e for e in store.load(vin, include_deleted=True) if e.get(\"id\") == id), None)","+    if event is None:","+        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}\", status_code=303)","+","+    fields_meta = event.get(\"fields_meta\") or {}","+    fields_disp = []","+    for key, val in (event.get(\"fields\") or {}).items():","+        spec = kd[\"fields\"].get(key, {})","+        label = spec.get(\"label\") or key.replace(\"_\", \" \").title()","+        fields_disp.append({","+            \"label\": label, \"value\": val, \"unit\": spec.get(\"unit\", \"\"),","+            \"from_photo\": fields_meta.get(key) == \"photo\",","+        })","+","+    return _page(request, \"m_confirm.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind,","+                kd=kd, event=event, fields_disp=fields_disp)","+","+","+# --- Snap & fill --------------------------------------------------------------","+","+","+@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/snap\", response_class=HTMLResponse)","+def snap_page(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:","+    hints = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": SNAP_HINT_LABELS.get(k, k.title())}","+            for k in SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET]","+    return _page(request, \"m_snap.html\", vin, \"add\", hints=hints)","+","+","+@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/snap\", response_class=HTMLResponse)","+async def snap_submit(request: Request, vin: str) -> RedirectResponse:","+    \"\"\"The no-JS (and no-vision-available) path: store the photo, then send","+    the person to the category/kind it's most likely about -- no field is","+    ever auto-filled here; only ``m.js``'s own client-side vision call does","+    that, and only when it actually has usable fields to offer.\"\"\"","+    form = await request.form()","+    hint = _field(form, \"hint\") or \"other\"","+    if hint not in SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET:","+        hint = \"other\"","+","+    media_id, error = await _upload_photo(vin, form, caption=f\"snap: {hint}\")","+    if error:","+        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/snap?error={quote('photo: ' + error)}\",","+                                status_code=303)","+    if not media_id:","+        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/snap?error=take+a+photo+first\", status_code=303)","+","+    category, kind = SNAP_FALLBACK_TARGET.get(hint, (None, None))","+    qs = f\"media_id={quote(media_id)}&hint={quote(hint)}\"","+    if category and kind:","+        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?{qs}\", status_code=303)","+    if category:","+        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}?{qs}\", status_code=303)","+    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/add?{qs}\", status_code=303)","+","+"," # --- Messages ------------------------------------------------------------------"," "," "]}],"originalFile":"\"\"\"``/m/{vin}`` -- \"Tell CUORE\": the phone-first page where an owner, driver\nor mechanic records what the car cannot discover on its own, and reads\nmessages/questions from CUORE and the mechanic.\n\nDeliberately its own minimal layout (``templates/m_*.html``, own\n``Jinja2Templates`` instance), same \"built concurrently with other agents\"\nposture as ``cuore.web.media_routes``/``timeline_routes``: no desktop\ntabs/hero, no dependency on ``cuore.web.routes``'s shared chrome, just a\nphone-width page with a bottom nav (Add / Messages / History).\n\n**Every record this page writes is ATTESTED, never a car measurement** --\nsee ``cuore/live/owner_events.py``'s docstring. The one-line footer on every\npage here says the same thing; do not remove it if these templates are\nedited later.\n\nWorks without JavaScript: every form is a plain ``<form method=\"post\">``\nthat redirects back to ``/m/{vin}#saved`` on success, same no-JS convention\n``cuore.web.media_routes.media_upload`` and ``inbox_routes`` use.\n\nRegistration note: ``cuore/app.py`` is owned by another agent. The one line\nneeded there, beside the other ``web`` routers::\n\n    app.include_router(owner_routes.router)\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport socket\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, RedirectResponse\nfrom fastapi.templating import Jinja2Templates\n\nfrom ..api.deps import require_token, settings_of\nfrom ..live import owner_events as store\nfrom ..services import owner_events_bridge as bridge\nfrom ..services.errors import BridgeError\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nTEMPLATE_DIR = HERE / \"templates\"\n\ntemplates = Jinja2Templates(directory=str(TEMPLATE_DIR))\n\nrouter = APIRouter(include_in_schema=False, dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n\n#: One pictogram-free label per category -- ``static/icons.svg`` has no\n#: symbol for any of these nine categories (its ``i-sys_*``/``i-symptom_*``\n#: set covers the systems graph and the driver symptom vocabulary, not\n#: owner-reported maintenance categories), so tiles render as plain labelled\n#: cards rather than inventing icons that would not match that file's house\n#: style. Flagged here rather than silently -- see the task note this\n#: satisfies.\nCATEGORY_ORDER = (\"fluids\", \"fuel\", \"battery_electrical\", \"tyres_wheels_brakes\",\n                  \"parts_repairs_elsewhere\", \"environment_exposure\", \"incidents\",\n                  \"driving_pattern\", \"cleaning_maintenance\")\n\n\ndef _page(request: Request, name: str, vin: str, active: str, **ctx: Any) -> HTMLResponse:\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, name, {\n        \"vin\": vin, \"active\": active, **ctx,\n    })\n\n\ndef _field(form: Any, name: str, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return str(form.get(name, default) or \"\").strip()\n\n\n# --- Add: category -> kind -> one-screen form --------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef home(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"Category tiles -- the landing/Add screen.\"\"\"\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    cats = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": tax[k][\"label\"], \"kind_count\": len(tax[k][\"kinds\"])}\n           for k in CATEGORY_ORDER if k in tax]\n    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params\n    return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=cats, saved=saved)\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef kinds_for_category(request: Request, vin: str, category: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    cat = tax.get(category)\n    if cat is None:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\",\n                     categories=[], error=f\"unknown category {category!r}\")\n    kinds = [{\"key\": k, \"label\": kd[\"label\"], \"why_it_matters\": kd[\"why_it_matters\"]}\n            for k, kd in cat[\"kinds\"].items()]\n    return _page(request, \"m_kinds.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category,\n                category_label=cat[\"label\"], kinds=kinds)\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef add_form(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return _page(request, \"m_categories.html\", vin, \"add\", categories=[], error=str(exc))\n    recents = {key: store.recent_values(vin, kind, key)\n               for key, spec in kd[\"fields\"].items() if spec.get(\"remember\")}\n    return _page(request, \"m_form.html\", vin, \"add\", category=category, kind=kind, kd=kd,\n                 recents=recents)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def add_submit(request: Request, vin: str, category: str, kind: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    form = await request.form()\n    try:\n        kd = store.kind_def(category, kind)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)\n\n    fields: dict[str, Any] = {}\n    for key in kd[\"fields\"]:\n        spec = kd[\"fields\"][key]\n        if spec[\"type\"] == \"bool\":\n            fields[key] = _field(form, key) in (\"on\", \"true\", \"1\", \"yes\")\n        else:\n            v = _field(form, key)\n            if v:\n                fields[key] = v\n\n    at = _field(form, \"at\") or None\n    by_role = _field(form, \"by_role\") or \"owner\"\n    by_name = _field(form, \"by_name\")\n    note = _field(form, \"note\")\n    odo_raw = _field(form, \"odometer_km\")\n    odometer_km: Optional[float] = None\n    if odo_raw:\n        try:\n            odometer_km = float(odo_raw)\n        except ValueError:\n            return RedirectResponse(\n                url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error=odometer+must+be+a+number\",\n                status_code=303)\n\n    try:\n        bridge.add(vin, category, kind, at=at, by_role=by_role, by_name=by_name,\n                  fields=fields, note=note, odometer_km=odometer_km)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(\n            url=f\"/m/{vin}/add/{category}/{kind}?error={quote(str(exc))}\", status_code=303)\n\n    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}#saved\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# --- Messages ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/messages\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef messages(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    data = bridge.messages(vin)\n    saved = \"saved\" in request.query_params\n    return _page(request, \"m_messages.html\", vin, \"messages\",\n                messages=data[\"messages\"], saved=saved)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/m/{vin}/messages/{id}/reply\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def reply(request: Request, vin: str, id: str) -> RedirectResponse:\n    form = await request.form()\n    text = _field(form, \"text\")\n    by = _field(form, \"by\") or \"owner\"\n    if not text:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages?error=a+reply+is+required\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    try:\n        bridge.reply_message(id, text, by=by)\n    except BridgeError as exc:\n        return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages?error={quote(str(exc))}\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    return RedirectResponse(url=f\"/m/{vin}/messages#saved\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# --- History --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/history\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef history(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    events = bridge.list_events(vin)[\"events\"]\n    events = sorted(events, key=lambda e: e.get(\"at\") or \"\", reverse=True)\n    rows = []\n    tax = store.TAXONOMY\n    for e in events:\n        cat = tax.get(e.get(\"category\", \"\"), {})\n        kd = cat.get(\"kinds\", {}).get(e.get(\"kind\", \"\"), {})\n        rows.append({**e, \"category_label\": cat.get(\"label\", e.get(\"category\")),\n                    \"kind_label\": kd.get(\"label\", e.get(\"kind\"))})\n    return _page(request, \"m_history.html\", vin, \"history\", events=rows)\n\n\n# --- QR / LAN link ---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _lan_ip() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Best-guess LAN-reachable address for this machine. Never sends\n    traffic -- the UDP ``connect`` just picks the outbound route/interface\n    without a packet leaving for a reserved address.\"\"\"\n    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)\n    try:\n        s.connect((\"10.255.255.255\", 1))\n        return s.getsockname()[0]\n    except OSError:\n        return \"127.0.0.1\"\n    finally:\n        s.close()\n\n\n@router.get(\"/m/{vin}/qr\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\ndef qr(request: Request, vin: str) -> HTMLResponse:\n    \"\"\"A QR of the LAN URL for this page -- only rendered when the server is\n    actually bound to something other than loopback (``CUORE_HOST``, aka\n    the bind setting; see ``cuore/config.py`` and the handbook note this\n    satisfies). The ``qrcode`` package is not in this project's venv, and\n    writing a from-scratch QR matrix generator is out of scope for this\n    pass, so the LAN URL is rendered as selectable text instead -- the\n    fallback the brief explicitly allows.\n    \"\"\"\n    settings = settings_of(request)\n    if not settings.lan_exposed:\n        return _page(request, \"m_qr.html\", vin, \"add\", lan_url=None,\n                    reason=\"This server is only reachable from this machine \"\n                          \"(loopback). Set CUORE_HOST=0.0.0.0 in the keep-alive \"\n                          \"to serve the LAN -- see docs/handbook/\"\n                          \"05-methods-and-gotchas.md.\")\n    url = f\"http://{_lan_ip()}:{settings.port}/m/{vin}\"\n    return _page(request, \"m_qr.html\", vin, \"add\", lan_url=url, reason=None)\n","userModified":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7e8d9abe-161f-4bde-bda4-77c024180239","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3fe49c97-4b72-4acd-b823-311bb38ca308","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
