{"parentUuid":"d3dbb180-0811-4c1d-a5ff-fc335c14c518","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a554eed87317d112b","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg15tEpgMiqs6kVg91wkb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ML162hDKzFyrmAqcneeVV4","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Mobile (\"Tell CUORE\") rebuild is complete, tested, and visually verified against the Ferrari benchmark.\n\n**fields_meta (both follow-ups addressed):**\n- `cuore/live/owner_events.py`: `add()` takes `fields_meta: {key: \"photo\"|\"typed\"}`, validated to this kind's real taxonomy fields and to those two values only; stored on the event. Docstring updated.\n- `cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.py`: `add()` threads it through.\n- `cuore/api/owner_events.py`: `OwnerEventRequest.fields_meta` added and passed to the bridge, so a native app (or anyone) can POST it directly; `GET`/`POST /owner/{vin}/events` return it on the row.\n- HTML form path feeds the same parameter via `source_<key>=photo` hidden inputs.\n\n**Rebuild** (`cuore/web/owner_routes.py`, `templates/m_home.html` new hero+quick-actions+messages-badge+everything-else, `m_fillup.html` new 3-tap flagship form, `m_confirm.html` new record card, `m_snap.html` new camera+hint screen, `m_form.html`/`m_kinds.html`/`m_categories.html` updated, `m_base.html` dark-pinned + intro-every-open, `static/m.css` full Ferrari-pass rewrite, `static/m.js` new): true black, hero name at 32-40px weight 300, big tabular odometer figure with 12px small-caps label, one-line verdict, 4 quick-action cards (Fill-up is the single red primary), messages badge, \"Everything else\" rows, underlined inputs (no boxes, units small after the figure), 12px letter-spaced chip labels with 200ms accent transition, toggle switch, record-card confirmation with 0.3s fade, Snap & fill wired to the now-live `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read` with full no-JS fallback.\n\n**Bug found and fixed during the Edge pass**: cuore.css's `input[type=text]` rule has the same CSS specificity as a bare class selector, so the original `.m-input` rule silently lost that fight and every free-text field rendered as a boxed input instead of underlined (number/date inputs were unaffected, which is what made it visible only on the station field). Fixed by using `input.m-input`/`textarea.m-textarea` selectors, which tie on specificity and win on source order. Confirmed by screenshot before/after.\n\n**Known limitation, not introduced by this work**: the pictogram `<use href=\"/static/icons.svg#...\">` sprite doesn't render in this repo's headless-Edge CDP test harness — confirmed via CDP diagnostics that the already-shipped `/v/{vin}` bench page (using the proven `cuore.web.icons.icon()` helper) shows the identical 0x0 `<use>` bounding box in the same harness, so this is a pre-existing, app-wide headless-Edge quirk, not a defect in the new markup. Icons should render normally in a real phone browser.\n\n**Tests**: `cuore/tests/check_owner_page.py` extended with 5 new sections (62 checks, 0 failures) covering home's 4 quick actions + intro overlay markup, fill-up octane/station last-used preselection, snap page camera input, `source_octane=photo` → `fields_meta.octane == \"photo\"` via the HTML form, the JSON API's fields_meta validation (unknown key and bad value both dropped), and the (now-live) vision endpoint's default \"unavailable\" response being handled gracefully by the snap page's own POST fallback. `check_screens.py` still passes (28 checks) — no regression.\n\n**Screenshots** (390x844, against a throwaway temp-state server, Edge cleaned up via `_edge_cleanup.kill_edge_profile`):\n- `C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\m_home_390x844.png`\n- `C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\m_fillup_390x844.png`\n\nKey files: `cuore/web/owner_routes.py`, `cuore/web/templates/m_home.html`, `m_fillup.html`, `m_confirm.html`, `m_snap.html`, `m_form.html`, `_camera_tile.html`, `cuore/web/static/m.css`, `cuore/web/static/m.js`, `cuore/live/owner_events.py`, `cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.py`, `cuore/api/owner_events.py`, `cuore/tests/check_owner_page.py`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":334,"cache_read_input_tokens":339645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":334,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ML162hDKzFyrmAqcneeVV4":{"message":"Mobile (\"Tell CUORE\") rebuild is complete, tested, and visually verified against the Ferrari benchmark.\n\n**fields_meta (both follow-ups addressed):**\n- `cuore/live/owner_events.py`: `add()` takes `fields_meta: {key: \"photo\"|\"typed\"}`, validated to this kind's real taxonomy fields and to those two values only; stored on the event. Docstring updated.\n- `cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.py`: `add()` threads it through.\n- `cuore/api/owner_events.py`: `OwnerEventRequest.fields_meta` added and passed to the bridge, so a native app (or anyone) can POST it directly; `GET`/`POST /owner/{vin}/events` return it on the row.\n- HTML form path feeds the same parameter via `source_<key>=photo` hidden inputs.\n\n**Rebuild** (`cuore/web/owner_routes.py`, `templates/m_home.html` new hero+quick-actions+messages-badge+everything-else, `m_fillup.html` new 3-tap flagship form, `m_confirm.html` new record card, `m_snap.html` new camera+hint screen, `m_form.html`/`m_kinds.html`/`m_categories.html` updated, `m_base.html` dark-pinned + intro-every-open, `static/m.css` full Ferrari-pass rewrite, `static/m.js` new): true black, hero name at 32-40px weight 300, big tabular odometer figure with 12px small-caps label, one-line verdict, 4 quick-action cards (Fill-up is the single red primary), messages badge, \"Everything else\" rows, underlined inputs (no boxes, units small after the figure), 12px letter-spaced chip labels with 200ms accent transition, toggle switch, record-card confirmation with 0.3s fade, Snap & fill wired to the now-live `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read` with full no-JS fallback.\n\n**Bug found and fixed during the Edge pass**: cuore.css's `input[type=text]` rule has the same CSS specificity as a bare class selector, so the original `.m-input` rule silently lost that fight and every free-text field rendered as a boxed input instead of underlined (number/date inputs were unaffected, which is what made it visible only on the station field). Fixed by using `input.m-input`/`textarea.m-textarea` selectors, which tie on specificity and win on source order. Confirmed by screenshot before/after.\n\n**Known limitation, not introduced by this work**: the pictogram `<use href=\"/static/icons.svg#...\">` sprite doesn't render in this repo's headless-Edge CDP test harness — confirmed via CDP diagnostics that the already-shipped `/v/{vin}` bench page (using the proven `cuore.web.icons.icon()` helper) shows the identical 0x0 `<use>` bounding box in the same harness, so this is a pre-existing, app-wide headless-Edge quirk, not a defect in the new markup. Icons should render normally in a real phone browser.\n\n**Tests**: `cuore/tests/check_owner_page.py` extended with 5 new sections (62 checks, 0 failures) covering home's 4 quick actions + intro overlay markup, fill-up octane/station last-used preselection, snap page camera input, `source_octane=photo` → `fields_meta.octane == \"photo\"` via the HTML form, the JSON API's fields_meta validation (unknown key and bad value both dropped), and the (now-live) vision endpoint's default \"unavailable\" response being handled gracefully by the snap page's own POST fallback. `check_screens.py` still passes (28 checks) — no regression.\n\n**Screenshots** (390x844, against a throwaway temp-state server, Edge cleaned up via `_edge_cleanup.kill_edge_profile`):\n- `C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\m_home_390x844.png`\n- `C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\m_fillup_390x844.png`\n\nKey files: `cuore/web/owner_routes.py`, `cuore/web/templates/m_home.html`, `m_fillup.html`, `m_confirm.html`, `m_snap.html`, `m_form.html`, `_camera_tile.html`, `cuore/web/static/m.css`, `cuore/web/static/m.js`, `cuore/live/owner_events.py`, `cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.py`, `cuore/api/owner_events.py`, `cuore/tests/check_owner_page.py`."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9460b7b0-f095-4d5d-8361-34435abd07e8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cg15tEYowpyKVMzDV7dhw","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a2dcf76f-b9f8-4b5f-8f62-8f9e78b02653","timestamp":"2026-10-13T23:14:12.428Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
